{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523712208,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f2c9e5001aXaMgAWKQhf1RX","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f2be56001ye4H6P2sAyLfLe","type":"tool","id":"call_f20ab40f7cae4dbdaf705ef1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/research.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, lines 1-179\n1: ---\n2: description: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Start Research Loop\n8: \n9: Thin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n10: \n11: ### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n12: \n13: - **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n14: - **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n15: - **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n16: - **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n17:   - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n18:   - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n19: \n20: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n23: \n24: Load the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n25: \n26: \n27: > **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n28: >\n29: > This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n30: >\n31: > **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n32: > 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n33: >    - `research_topic`\n34: >    - `spec_folder`\n35: >    - `execution_mode`\n36: >    - `maxIterations`\n37: >    - `convergenceThreshold`\n38: >    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n39: >    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n40: > 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n41: >    - Auto: `deep-research-auto.yaml`\n42: >    - Confirm: `deep-research-confirm.yaml`\n43: > 3. Execute the YAML workflow step by step using those resolved values\n44: >\n45: > This command is **general-agent based** — it orchestrates the deep-research loop. The Unified Setup Phase (the BLOCKED gate) is a HARD BLOCK; it may not be skipped.\n46: \n47: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt in the presentation contract MUST be the first visible response. For `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated setup prompt by default; use the auto setup resolution rules in the presentation contract and fail fast when required fields cannot be resolved.\n48: \n49: > **Canonical mode syntax:** use attached command suffixes (`/deep:research:auto`, `/deep:research:confirm`).\n50: \n51: > **Note:** Late-INIT `spec.md` detection and bounded `spec.md` mutations follow\n52: > `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md`.\n53: > Acquire `{spec_folder}/research/.deep-research.lock` before `folder_state` classification and keep `research/research.md` as the source of truth for any generated findings sync.\n54: > Targeted strict validation after deep-research spec mutations uses the Node validation orchestrator.\n55: \n56: ### AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION DIRECTIVE (:auto)\n57: \n58: > Read this first. It is an imperative to you, the executor — not background information.\n59: \n60: You were invoked via `opencode run --command deep/research` with the `:auto` suffix and a bound spec_folder and target in your message. The `:auto` suffix plus the bound spec_folder mean setup is ALREADY resolved. Therefore:\n61: \n62: - DO NOT emit the consolidated setup question (target/mode, research topic, Spec Folder A/B/C/D, execution mode, max iterations, executor). The bound spec_folder is your write authority; do not ask which spec folder should own the writes.\n63: - DO NOT halt for the repo-wide `CLAUDE.md` Gate-3 documentation gate. Under AUTONOMOUS execution with a validated prebound spec folder, Gate 3 is already satisfied by that folder (the prebound spec folder is your write authority).\n64: - PROCEED immediately: load the auto workflow YAML and dispatch the `deep-research` agent to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n65: - DISPATCH ONLY: You dispatch `deep-research` to run one iteration.\n66:   You do NOT read, edit, patch or run the research loop over the target yourself.\n67:   The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself.\n68:   It owns setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence checks, synthesis and all loop-level artifact writes.\n69:   The `deep-research` leaf owns only its own single-iteration artifacts.\n70:   Mixing your inline work with the dispatch is a route violation.\n71: - ROUTE PROOF: dispatch through the auto workflow with its prompt pack so `deep-research` writes each iteration state record with the route-proof fields present — `target_agent: \"deep-research\"`, `resolved_route`, `agent_definition_loaded: true`, and `mode: \"research\"`. A completed run whose iteration state records omit these fields is an incomplete delegation and does not pass.\n72: \n73: Your job is to DISPATCH `deep-research` to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n74: You do NOT run the loop yourself.\n75: You do NOT review or analyze this contract.\n76: You do NOT summarize this contract.\n77: The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself.\n78: It owns setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence, synthesis and loop-level writes.\n79: This contract is your instruction set.\n80: The research target is the bound spec_folder/target named in your message, never this document.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n85: \n86: | Purpose | Asset |\n87: |---------|-------|\n88: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt` |\n89: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n90: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n95: \n96: 1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for attached suffixes: `:auto` sets `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS`; `:confirm` sets `execution_mode = INTERACTIVE`; no suffix sets `execution_mode = ASK`.\n97: 2. Treat `--max-iterations`, `--convergence`, `--lineage-timeout-hours`, `--stop-policy`, `--dry-run`, `--spec-folder`, `--executor`, `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count`, `--executors`, `--concurrency`, and `--no-resource-map` as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n98: 3. For `:auto`, resolve setup from `$ARGUMENTS` flags, any `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker block, scope-extracted spec-folder paths, and the presentation contract's default resolution table. When all required fields are resolved, persist `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json`, bind runtime YAML placeholders, and load `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n99: 4. In `:auto`, ask a targeted Tier-2 question only for `spec_folder` when the topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity; use the named-missing-inputs fail-fast format from the auto-mode contract and do not load YAML.\n100: 5. For `:confirm`, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to bind missing setup values, then load `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml`.\n101: 6. For no suffix, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to choose execution mode and bind missing setup values, then route the resolved interactive choice to the matching YAML.\n102: 7. Lightweight read-only discovery for related spec folders or prior memory may support setup, but it must feed the single consolidated prompt and never split setup questions.\n103: 8. After the selected workflow asset is loaded, execute it step by step using the resolved setup values.\n104: \n105: ### Workflow Flag Surface\n106: \n107: The argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every flag below\n108: is a workflow input, never an execution mode, and the presentation asset owns how each one binds\n109: into `config`.\n110: \n111: | Flag | Value | Effect |\n112: |------|-------|--------|\n113: | `--spec-folder` | `PATH` | Binds the packet that owns this run's writes. |\n114: | `--max-iterations` | `N` | Hard ceiling on loop iterations. |\n115: | `--convergence` | `N` | Threshold the loop must clear before convergence may stop it. |\n116: | `--convergence-mode` | `default` \\| `off` \\| `sliding-window` \\| `divergent` | `default` keeps the anti-convergence `minIterations` floor. `off` disables convergence-driven STOP while max-iterations, pause and halt stay active. `sliding-window` scores novelty over a bounded window, five snapshots by default, on the ordinary legal-stop path. `divergent` sends a `composite_converged` or `all_questions_answered` stop into a one-round three-seat Council pivot instead of ending the run, at proportionally higher cost. |\n117: | `--lineage-timeout-hours` | `N` | See Lineage Timeout Flag below. |\n118: | `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n119: | `--no-resource-map` | no value | Suppresses the `research/resource-map.md` write; `research.md` still emits. |\n120: | `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n121: | `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. |\n122: | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n123: | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n124: \n125: Fan-out policy: zero or one `--executor` runs the single-executor path, and so does an\n126: `--executors` matrix that expands to exactly one lineage. Its `iterations` value binds to\n127: `config.maxIterations`, and its executor settings populate `config.executor`. Two or more\n128: `--executor` flags, a matrix expanding to two or more lineages, or any `--count` above 1\n129: selects fan-out. A direct call of the fan-out runner that expands to one research or review\n130: lineage is refused and names this workflow instead, because the runner alone skips packet\n131: init, synthesis and save. Under `:auto` a `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block\n132: in the prompt body binds the same values without an interactive prompt.\n133: \n134: ### Lineage Timeout Flag\n135: \n136: `--lineage-timeout-hours <N>` optionally narrows the per-lineage wall-clock timeout ceiling below the default 4 hours; values above the hard 4-hour maximum are rejected, and omitting the flag keeps the 4h default.\n137: \n138: ### Stop Policy Flag\n139: \n140: `--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence or `config.maxIterations`, whichever comes first; `max-iterations` treats convergence as telemetry only and forces the loop to continue until `config.maxIterations`, which is useful for forced-depth runs.\n141: \n142: ### Dry-Run Flag\n143: \n144: `--dry-run` is a first-class flag on the confirm flow, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n145: \n146: When `dry_run=true`, the confirm YAML emits `dry_run_halt` JSONL preview lines to terminal output instead of appending to the live state log, and halts before executor dispatch, persistent state mutation, reducer refresh, or child-lineage spawn.\n147: A fresh packet will stop at the first persistent state boundary.\n148: An existing packet can read current state and convergence signals, render the next prompt for preview, then stop before dispatch.\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n153: \n154: | Mode | Target |\n155: |------|----------|\n156: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n157: | `:confirm` or interactive choice | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n162: \n163: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt`:\n164: \n165: - Startup-question wording, consolidated setup prompt text, and reply format examples.\n166: - `:auto` pre-bound setup answer schema, default resolution table, targeted-ask rules, and fail-fast display references.\n167: - Dashboard/checkpoint layout, workflow overview display, convergence-threshold explanation, and user-facing examples.\n168: - Success and failure result templates, error-handling display, and memory-integration result wording.\n169: - Next-step suggestions, command-chain wording, skill-reference text, and offline optimization notes.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n174: \n175: The selected YAML workflow initializes deep-research state, dispatches fresh `@deep-research` LEAF agents per iteration, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `{artifact_dir}/research.md`, optionally emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md`, and refreshes continuity through canonical spec docs. This command does not proceed to implementation.\n176: \n177: For code review and quality auditing, route to `/deep:review`. Research path: `/deep:research` → `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`; review path: `/deep:review` → (if issues) `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`.\n178: \n179: Each iteration's prompt tells the writer that its `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags are checked by the `SOURCE_TAGS` rule. That rule runs in the next `/speckit:*` validation rather than inside this workflow, whose validation calls list their own rules. A resolved tag proves only that the path and line exist.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/research.md, lines 1-179\n1: ---\n2: description: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Start Research Loop\n8: \n9: Thin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n10: \n11: ### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n12: \n13: - **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n14: - **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n15: - **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n16: - **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n17:   - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n18:   - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n19: \n20: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n21: \n22: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n23: \n24: Load the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n25: \n26: \n27: > **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n28: >\n29: > This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n30: >\n31: > **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n32: > 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n33: >    - `research_topic`\n34: >    - `spec_folder`\n35: >    - `execution_mode`\n36: >    - `maxIterations`\n37: >    - `convergenceThreshold`\n38: >    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n39: >    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n40: > 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n41: >    - Auto: `deep-research-auto.yaml`\n42: >    - Confirm: `deep-research-confirm.yaml`\n43: > 3. Execute the YAML workflow step by step using those resolved values\n44: >\n45: > This command is **general-agent based** — it orchestrates the deep-research loop. The Unified Setup Phase (the BLOCKED gate) is a HARD BLOCK; it may not be skipped.\n46: \n47: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt in the presentation contract MUST be the first visible response. For `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated setup prompt by default; use the auto setup resolution rules in the presentation contract and fail fast when required fields cannot be resolved.\n48: \n49: > **Canonical mode syntax:** use attached command suffixes (`/deep:research:auto`, `/deep:research:confirm`).\n50: \n51: > **Note:** Late-INIT `spec.md` detection and bounded `spec.md` mutations follow\n52: > `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md`.\n53: > Acquire `{spec_folder}/research/.deep-research.lock` before `folder_state` classification and keep `research/research.md` as the source of truth for any generated findings sync.\n54: > Targeted strict validation after deep-research spec mutations uses the Node validation orchestrator.\n55: \n56: ### AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION DIRECTIVE (:auto)\n57: \n58: > Read this first. It is an imperative to you, the executor — not background information.\n59: \n60: You were invoked via `opencode run --command deep/research` with the `:auto` suffix and a bound spec_folder and target in your message. The `:auto` suffix plus the bound spec_folder mean setup is ALREADY resolved. Therefore:\n61: \n62: - DO NOT emit the consolidated setup question (target/mode, research topic, Spec Folder A/B/C/D, execution mode, max iterations, executor). The bound spec_folder is your write authority; do not ask which spec folder should own the writes.\n63: - DO NOT halt for the repo-wide `CLAUDE.md` Gate-3 documentation gate. Under AUTONOMOUS execution with a validated prebound spec folder, Gate 3 is already satisfied by that folder (the prebound spec folder is your write authority).\n64: - PROCEED immediately: load the auto workflow YAML and dispatch the `deep-research` agent to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n65: - DISPATCH ONLY: You dispatch `deep-research` to run one iteration.\n66:   You do NOT read, edit, patch or run the research loop over the target yourself.\n67:   The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself.\n68:   It owns setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence checks, synthesis and all loop-level artifact writes.\n69:   The `deep-research` leaf owns only its own single-iteration artifacts.\n70:   Mixing your inline work with the dispatch is a route violation.\n71: - ROUTE PROOF: dispatch through the auto workflow with its prompt pack so `deep-research` writes each iteration state record with the route-proof fields present — `target_agent: \"deep-research\"`, `resolved_route`, `agent_definition_loaded: true`, and `mode: \"research\"`. A completed run whose iteration state records omit these fields is an incomplete delegation and does not pass.\n72: \n73: Your job is to DISPATCH `deep-research` to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n74: You do NOT run the loop yourself.\n75: You do NOT review or analyze this contract.\n76: You do NOT summarize this contract.\n77: The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself.\n78: It owns setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence, synthesis and loop-level writes.\n79: This contract is your instruction set.\n80: The research target is the bound spec_folder/target named in your message, never this document.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n85: \n86: | Purpose | Asset |\n87: |---------|-------|\n88: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt` |\n89: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n90: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n95: \n96: 1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for attached suffixes: `:auto` sets `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS`; `:confirm` sets `execution_mode = INTERACTIVE`; no suffix sets `execution_mode = ASK`.\n97: 2. Treat `--max-iterations`, `--convergence`, `--lineage-timeout-hours`, `--stop-policy`, `--dry-run`, `--spec-folder`, `--executor`, `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count`, `--executors`, `--concurrency`, and `--no-resource-map` as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n98: 3. For `:auto`, resolve setup from `$ARGUMENTS` flags, any `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker block, scope-extracted spec-folder paths, and the presentation contract's default resolution table. When all required fields are resolved, persist `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json`, bind runtime YAML placeholders, and load `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n99: 4. In `:auto`, ask a targeted Tier-2 question only for `spec_folder` when the topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity; use the named-missing-inputs fail-fast format from the auto-mode contract and do not load YAML.\n100: 5. For `:confirm`, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to bind missing setup values, then load `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml`.\n101: 6. For no suffix, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to choose execution mode and bind missing setup values, then route the resolved interactive choice to the matching YAML.\n102: 7. Lightweight read-only discovery for related spec folders or prior memory may support setup, but it must feed the single consolidated prompt and never split setup questions.\n103: 8. After the selected workflow asset is loaded, execute it step by step using the resolved setup values.\n104: \n105: ### Workflow Flag Surface\n106: \n107: The argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every flag below\n108: is a workflow input, never an execution mode, and the presentation asset owns how each one binds\n109: into `config`.\n110: \n111: | Flag | Value | Effect |\n112: |------|-------|--------|\n113: | `--spec-folder` | `PATH` | Binds the packet that owns this run's writes. |\n114: | `--max-iterations` | `N` | Hard ceiling on loop iterations. |\n115: | `--convergence` | `N` | Threshold the loop must clear before convergence may stop it. |\n116: | `--convergence-mode` | `default` \\| `off` \\| `sliding-window` \\| `divergent` | `default` keeps the anti-convergence `minIterations` floor. `off` disables convergence-driven STOP while max-iterations, pause and halt stay active. `sliding-window` scores novelty over a bounded window, five snapshots by default, on the ordinary legal-stop path. `divergent` sends a `composite_converged` or `all_questions_answered` stop into a one-round three-seat Council pivot instead of ending the run, at proportionally higher cost. |\n117: | `--lineage-timeout-hours` | `N` | See Lineage Timeout Flag below. |\n118: | `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n119: | `--no-resource-map` | no value | Suppresses the `research/resource-map.md` write; `research.md` still emits. |\n120: | `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n121: | `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. |\n122: | `--executors` | `JSON` | Declares the executor matrix in one value; one expanded lineage selects `config.executor`, while two or more select `config.fanout`. |\n123: | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n124: \n125: Fan-out policy: zero or one `--executor` runs the single-executor path, and so does an\n126: `--executors` matrix that expands to exactly one lineage. Its `iterations` value binds to\n127: `config.maxIterations`, and its executor settings populate `config.executor`. Two or more\n128: `--executor` flags, a matrix expanding to two or more lineages, or any `--count` above 1\n129: selects fan-out. A direct call of the fan-out runner that expands to one research or review\n130: lineage is refused and names this workflow instead, because the runner alone skips packet\n131: init, synthesis and save. Under `:auto` a `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block\n132: in the prompt body binds the same values without an interactive prompt.\n133: \n134: ### Lineage Timeout Flag\n135: \n136: `--lineage-timeout-hours <N>` optionally narrows the per-lineage wall-clock timeout ceiling below the default 4 hours; values above the hard 4-hour maximum are rejected, and omitting the flag keeps the 4h default.\n137: \n138: ### Stop Policy Flag\n139: \n140: `--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence or `config.maxIterations`, whichever comes first; `max-iterations` treats convergence as telemetry only and forces the loop to continue until `config.maxIterations`, which is useful for forced-depth runs.\n141: \n142: ### Dry-Run Flag\n143: \n144: `--dry-run` is a first-class flag on the confirm flow, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n145: \n146: When `dry_run=true`, the confirm YAML emits `dry_run_halt` JSONL preview lines to terminal output instead of appending to the live state log, and halts before executor dispatch, persistent state mutation, reducer refresh, or child-lineage spawn.\n147: A fresh packet will stop at the first persistent state boundary.\n148: An existing packet can read current state and convergence signals, render the next prompt for preview, then stop before dispatch.\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n153: \n154: | Mode | Target |\n155: |------|----------|\n156: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n157: | `:confirm` or interactive choice | `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n162: \n163: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt`:\n164: \n165: - Startup-question wording, consolidated setup prompt text, and reply format examples.\n166: - `:auto` pre-bound setup answer schema, default resolution table, targeted-ask rules, and fail-fast display references.\n167: - Dashboard/checkpoint layout, workflow overview display, convergence-threshold explanation, and user-facing examples.\n168: - Success and failure result templates, error-handling display, and memory-integration result wording.\n169: - Next-step suggestions, command-chain wording, skill-reference text, and offline optimization notes.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n174: \n175: The selected YAML workflow initializes deep-research state, dispatches fresh `@deep-research` LEAF agents per iteration, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `{artifact_dir}/research.md`, optionally emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md`, and refreshes continuity through canonical spec docs. This command does not proceed to implementation.\n176: \n177: For code review and quality auditing, route to `/deep:review`. Research path: `/deep:research` → `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`; review path: `/deep:review` → (if issues) `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`.\n178: \n179: Each iteration's prompt tells the writer that its `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags are checked by the `SOURCE_TAGS` rule. That rule runs in the next `/speckit:*` validation rather than inside this workflow, whose validation calls list their own rules. A resolved tag proves only that the path and line exist."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523711973,"end":1794523712208}}}}
