. GOOD: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives in `logs/archive` and exits 0. WEAK: The work is done. -->\n89: \n90: - [ ] Strict validation of this packet prints `RESULT: PASSED` for the parent and all eight phases, each Complete.\n91: - [ ] The advisor suite (`npx vitest run`) reports 0 failed, typed recall is 24 of 44 or more and false offers are 0 of 35.\n92: - [ ] The behaviour summary prints a before and an after start rate for claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh, and each unsafe start after has a fix or a reason in this log.\n93: - [ ] A `/deep:review` loop over the packet code has converged with 0 open P0 and P1 findings.\n94: - [ ] A `/deep:research` loop on UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness has converged, with each recommendation built in a new phase or declined with a reason.\n95: - [ ] `/local-skilled-alignment` on the branch reports 0 P0 and 0 P1 findings.\n96: - [ ] The branch sits on `origin/main`, clean and unpushed, with each item waiting on the operator in this log.\n97: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: <!-- ANCHOR:log -->\n102: ## 4. LOG\n103: <!-- FILL: Record each step with its command output. Keep this table current. GOOD: T001 Done. `ls logs/archive | wc -l` printed 3. WEAK: Progress is good. -->\n104: \n105: Everything below is VOLATILE. It is not part of the directive, it is not copied\n106: into the objective, and it is expected to grow. Progress, evidence, deviations\n107: and findings belong here.\n108: \n109: ### Progress\n110: \n111: | Item | State | Evidence |\n112: |------|-------|----------|\n113: | Phases 001 to 004 | Done | Each validates with `RESULT: PASSED`, status Complete |\n114: | Phases 005 to 008 | In Progress | Planned and committed 2026-11-12. Phase 007 harness built, smoke run three in flight |\n115: | Rebase onto main | Done | 2026-11-12, full suite 167 files 1,478 passed |\n116: | Phase 007 smoke run | Done | Third run: all six runtimes ran in arenas and scored, start rate 0 of 1 each, one capped (opencode). runs-smoke.jsonl |\n117: | Ungated setup while the before arm runs | Done | 005 wave 0 captures, 007 T016-T021, 008 measurement script, commits d8797702e8 and 49281dd652 |\n118: \n119: ### Deviations and findings\n120: \n121: | Item | Note |\n122: |------|------|\n123: | Operator answers before this goal | 57 answers are recorded in `decision-record.md` files of this packet and stay binding |\n124: <!-- /ANCHOR:log -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523733955,"end":1794523734261}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794523735965,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f3279d0019ObddqWPpN16Ws","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f3189300112EAeGyvynLnjI","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":798,"output":109,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":58624,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794523738270,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f3309e001XdPjxigndu6kew","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f327a2001PYn4n0xSyepUu3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523739434,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f3322e001NI9IyV72l1IZbk","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f327a2001PYn4n0xSyepUu3","type":"tool","id":"call_4862e1453fd741a389a79009","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 1-173\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and its hooks |\n25: | **Storage** | None. The command table is generated source, and the bridge file is JSON |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four design questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog, each the recommended option, and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n40: - [ ] The coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done. No code task starts before it.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the pinned capture, the default command capture, the rollup, six live brief heads, the sk-doc reach check, three hook timing runs and the suite.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] The schema test, the six golden briefs and the reach check with real embeddings pass. `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: One generated table, many readers. Nothing hand-keeps a command string or a policy.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Command table** (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, generated by `derive-command-bridges.cjs`): `COMMAND_ROWS` maps every id a scorer can return for a command entry, the TypeScript id, the Python id and the inventory id, to `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }`. `COMMAND_POLICIES` maps each runnable string to its policy. Without it each reader would rebuild the join from `commandPolicies`, the doctor details and the projection.\n59: - **Public fields** (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): `publicRecommendation` copies `kind` and, for a row found in `COMMAND_ROWS`, sets `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. `enrichCompiledRoutes` adds the policy of an attached command and reads the already-offered set from the `command` fields instead of from bridge keywords.\n60: - **Brief head** (`ADV/lib/render.ts`): a recommendation with a command renders `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)`, where the owner is `ownerSkillId` or, for a hub with an attached command, the hub id. Fields win, and `COMMAND_ROWS` fills a missing field by id, which covers an older daemon and the Python subprocess path.\n61: - **Degraded contract** (`ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`): `degradedRecommendations` keeps a command row's fields only when its bare slash command appears in the prompt, and otherwise replaces it with its owner skill.\n62: - **Reach check** (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs`): `rankShippedFleet` counts a hit when the first shipped entry is the hub or is a command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the hub.\n63: \n64: ### Data Flow\n65: `command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n113: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n114: \n115: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n116: |-----------|-------|-------|\n117: | Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n118: | Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n119: | Manual | `save context`, `/speckit:plan` and readme CLI checks, six live hook heads, the reach check with Ollama, three hook timing runs | The advisor CLI, the phase 003 timing script copied into `scratch/` |\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n126: \n127: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n128: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n129: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` | Internal | Green: generated today | No policy to show |\n130: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the `command` field | Internal | Green: in code today | No attached command to label |\n131: | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text` | External | Green: the tags call listed `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on 2026-11-12 | The reach proof for REQ-018 cannot run |\n132: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n133: | Phase 007 before-measurement on the branch tip | Ordering | Open: waits on the coordinator's confirmation | Every code task waits, wave 0 may run |\n134: | The `nm-sk-doc-01` source trace | Internal | Open: the token sources are UNKNOWN until T055 | The fix task T056 cannot name its file |\n135: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n140: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n141: \n142: - **Trigger**: a pinned number moves, a default capture number moves, a false offer appears or the suite fails after the waves that touch scoring ids.\n143: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits, run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `npm run build` in `ADV`. Then confirm `--check` prints `fresh` and the pinned capture prints `[159,50,20,5]`. The id rename and the relabel revert together because they land in the same commits.\n144: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n150: \n151: ```\n152: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n153: ```\n154: \n155: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n156: |-------|------------|--------|\n157: | Setup | Phase 004 shipped code | Implementation |\n158: | Implementation | The before numbers, the operator answers and the phase 007 confirmation | Verification |\n159: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 006 |\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n165: ## DECISIONS ALREADY MADE\n166: \n167: No new decision is recorded here. The phase follows these, all in `../decision-record.md` or the review:\n168: - D1 (Q006): a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started. The `start` word in the head carries it.\n169: - D2 (Q007, Q011): the model picks freely between the command and the skill. The head names both.\n170: - The review's R3 field set and the L12 rule of no consequence line, read in `synthesis-review.md` section 3.\n171: \n172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md, lines 1-173\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\"\n3: description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"recommendation contract and brief plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and its hooks |\n25: | **Storage** | None. The command table is generated source, and the bridge file is JSON |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the Python test script, the routing-accuracy captures and the sk-doc reach check |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four design questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog, each the recommended option, and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n40: - [ ] The coordinator confirms that phase 007's before-measurement on the branch tip is done. No code task starts before it.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the pinned capture, the default command capture, the rollup, six live brief heads, the sk-doc reach check, three hook timing runs and the suite.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] The schema test, the six golden briefs and the reach check with real embeddings pass. `save context` returns one entry carrying `/speckit:save`. `npm test` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.