e deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n66: \n67: ### Head Form\n68: The six golden heads, one per family, each followed by the existing `\\nDirectives:` block:\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n72: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop → /deep:research (ask) 0.82/0.16 pass.\n73: Advisor: live; use sk-design → /design:chart (start) 0.90/0.12 pass.\n74: Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.\n75: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n76: Advisor: live; use sk-prompt → /prompt:improve (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n77: ```\n78: \n79: The policies come from `commandPolicies` today. A recommendation with no command keeps today's `use <skill>` head. A command row with no table entry keeps its sanitized id. A missing policy drops the parenthesis.\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n85: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n86: \n87: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n88: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n89: | `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` and `renderDoctorCommandStrings` | Doctor-only runnable labels | Replace with `COMMAND_ROWS`, keep `doctorCommandString` as a wrapper | `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS\"` prints nothing and the doctor tests pass |\n90: | `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` | Already-offered set from bridge keywords | Read the `command` fields instead | `tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` |\n91: | `recommendationFromCli` | Keeps `command` only, forces `kind: 'skill'` | Keep `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` | Hook fallback tests |\n92: | `degradedRecommendations` | Copies skill id and scores | Apply the degraded contract | New degraded test |\n93: | `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94: | `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95: | Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n96: | `AGENTS.md`, Gate 2 and pointers | Phase 006 | Unchanged | `git diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md` |\n97: | `Also:` companion line | Doctor-only second command | Unchanged | Doctor brief tests |\n98: \n99: Matrix axes for the renderer: a field present or absent, an id in the table or not, a policy present or absent, ambiguous or not. Every axis has one test row.\n100: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n101: \n102: ---\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n105: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n106: \n107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n113: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n114: \n115: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n116: |-----------|-------|-------|\n117: | Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n118: | Integration | The pinned capture, the default command capture, the derive check, the rollup and the Python test script | The capture scripts, `jq`, `python3` |\n119: | Manual | `save context`, `/speckit:plan` and readme CLI checks, six live hook heads, the reach check with Ollama, three hook timing runs | The advisor CLI, the phase 003 timing script copied into `scratch/` |\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n126: \n127: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n128: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n129: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` | Internal | Green: generated today | No policy to show |\n130: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the `command` field | Internal | Green: in code today | No attached command to label |\n131: | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text` | External | Green: the tags call listed `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on 2026-11-12 | The reach proof for REQ-018 cannot run |\n132: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n133: | Phase 007 before-measurement on the branch tip | Ordering | Open: waits on the coordinator's confirmation | Every code task waits, wave 0 may run |\n134: | The `nm-sk-doc-01` source trace | Internal | Open: the token sources are UNKNOWN until T055 | The fix task T056 cannot name its file |\n135: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n140: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n141: \n142: - **Trigger**: a pinned number moves, a default capture number moves, a false offer appears or the suite fails after the waves that touch scoring ids.\n143: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits, run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `npm run build` in `ADV`. Then confirm `--check` prints `fresh` and the pinned capture prints `[159,50,20,5]`. The id rename and the relabel revert together because they land in the same commits.\n144: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n150: \n151: ```\n152: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n153: ```\n154: \n155: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n156: |-------|------------|--------|\n157: | Setup | Phase 004 shipped code | Implementation |\n158: | Implementation | The before numbers, the operator answers and the phase 007 confirmation | Verification |\n159: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 006 |\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n165: ## DECISIONS ALREADY MADE\n166: \n167: No new decision is recorded here. The phase follows these, all in `../decision-record.md` or the review:\n168: - D1 (Q006): a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started. The `start` word in the head carries it.\n169: - D2 (Q007, Q011): the model picks freely between the command and the skill. The head names both.\n170: - The review's R3 field set and the L12 rule of no consequence line, read in `synthesis-review.md` section 3.\n171: \n172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n173: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523738670,"end":1794523739434}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523739442,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f3336e001J6uc7QSBDo9DF1","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f327a2001PYn4n0xSyepUu3","type":"tool","id":"call_47bc42c45816420f9cfe7a7f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 1-256\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Add one Gate 2 bullet for a surfaced command, copy it into the Cursor rule through the existing pointer generator, hand a hub mode to its command, name the plan workflow in the Gate 3 notice and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Markdown instruction files, CommonJS generators, one ES module, one Bash script and TypeScript in the advisor |\n24: | **Framework** | The `AGENTS.md` manifest and check engine under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, the spec-kit runtime mirrors and the system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV`) |\n25: | **Storage** | None. Every output is a tracked text file |\n26: | **Testing** | `/doctor:agents-md check`, the manifest check, the rule-copy canary, Vitest in `ADV` and in the spec-kit CLI, `node --test` for the spec gate |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The rule lives once, in Gate 2 of `AGENTS.md`. Every other surface either copies it through a generator that checks the copy, or points at the command document from where a model already is: the hub router after it picks a mode, the Gate 3 notice before the first write and the brief in a child session. Nothing in scoring moves.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12. `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 shipped, and the Claude hook's first line for `create a readme for the utils folder` shows `/create:readme` and a policy word (T002). Without it only the REQ-004 tasks wait.\n40: - [ ] The before numbers in `spec.md` Measured Behavior still hold (T001).\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `/doctor:agents-md check` prints `STATUS=OK`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n128: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n129: \n130: - **Trigger**: `/doctor:agents-md check` not `OK`, the pointer check failing, a failing suite or a behaviour run in phase 007 showing the bullet steers turns wrongly.\n131: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commit, then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` so the derived copy and the Cursor rule match the reverted `AGENTS.md`. Finish with `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n132: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n133: \n134: ---\n135: \n136: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n137: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n138: \n139: ```\n140: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n141: ```\n142: \n143: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n144: |-------|------------|--------|\n145: | Setup | Operator answers, phase 005 for REQ-004 only | Implementation |\n146: | Implementation | The before numbers | Verification |\n147: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 007 |\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n153: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n154: \n155: Every ADR below records an operator decision already made. None is new.\n156: \n157: ### ADR-001: The command path and the skill path are both whole workflows\n158: \n159: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Looser: AI picks freely\" (`../decision-record.md` Q011, D2)\n160: \n161: **Context**: The review's Gate 2 text and its G1 router rule make the command the workflow a model must follow.\n162: \n163: **Decision**: The Gate 2 bullet and the three router bullets name the command beside the skill. A model picks either and follows it whole, never an improvised mix. The operator approved the exact Gate 2 text on 2026-11-12, \"Command beside the skill (Recommended)\".\n164: \n165: **Consequences**:\n166: - The command is a suggestion the model may decline. The `COMMAND:` token records `declined` so phase 007 can count it.\n167: - A `command: null` mode keeps its packet as the only path.\n168: \n169: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n170: - Command as the default entry with the skill for partial work: the operator chose the looser reading over it (Q011).\n171: \n172: ### ADR-002: A started command runs without `:auto`\n173: \n174: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Start it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q006, D1)\n175: \n176: **Context**: Twenty commands carry the `start` policy, and their own setup asks for a mode, Gate 3 and a yes at an irreversible step.\n177: \n178: **Decision**: The bullet defines `start` as starting the command without `:auto`, so its setup asks.\n179: \n180: **Consequences**:\n181: - A typed `:auto` or an explicit instruction still wins (L5).\n182: - Whether a started command keeps to its setup is phase 007's G2 check.\n183: \n184: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n185: - Ask before every write command: rejected by the operator (Q006).\n186: \n187: ### ADR-003: A deep loop is always asked first\n188: \n189: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Only on depth wording (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q008, D3)\n190: \n191: **Context**: The three `/deep:*` commands carry the `ask` policy in `commandPolicies` today.\n192: \n193: **Decision**: The bullet's `ask` sentence covers them, and no deep-loop clause is added to `AGENTS.md`. The deep-loop router bullet notes that `deep-research/SKILL.md` names its command as its only entry.\n194: \n195: **Consequences**:\n196: - No bytes spent on a deep-loop rule in the delivery prefix.\n197: \n198: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n199: - A separate deep-loop clause in Gate 2: it would restate the policy word.\n200: \n201: ### ADR-004: The invocation table covers the 44 tracked commands\n202: \n203: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"No, exclude it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q012, D5)\n204: \n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n255: - Keep the label with a retired list: the operator chose removal.\n256: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 1-256\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Add one Gate 2 bullet for a surfaced command, copy it into the Cursor rule through the existing pointer generator, hand a hub mode to its command, name the plan workflow in the Gate 3 notice and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Markdown instruction files, CommonJS generators, one ES module, one Bash script and TypeScript in the advisor |\n24: | **Framework** | The `AGENTS.md` manifest and check engine under `.skilled/commands/doctor/`, the spec-kit runtime mirrors and the system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV`) |\n25: | **Storage** | None. Every output is a tracked text file |\n26: | **Testing** | `/doctor:agents-md check`, the manifest check, the rule-copy canary, Vitest in `ADV` and in the spec-kit CLI, `node --test` for the spec gate |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The rule lives once, in Gate 2 of `AGENTS.md`. Every other surface either copies it through a generator that checks the copy, or points at the command document from where a model already is: the hub router after it picks a mode, the Gate 3 notice before the first write and the brief in a child session. Nothing in scoring moves.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12. `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 shipped, and the Claude hook's first line for `create a readme for the utils folder` shows `/create:readme` and a policy word (T002). Without it only the REQ-004 tasks wait.\n40: - [ ] The before numbers in `spec.md` Measured Behavior still hold (T001).\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `/doctor:agents-md check` prints `STATUS=OK`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n128: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n129: \n130: - **Trigger**: `/doctor:agents-md check` not `OK`, the pointer check failing, a failing suite or a behaviour run in phase 007 showing the bullet steers turns wrongly.\n131: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commit, then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` and `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` so the derived copy and the Cursor rule match the reverted `AGENTS.md`. Finish with `/doctor:agents-md check`.\n132: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n133: \n134: ---\n135: \n136: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n137: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n138: \n139: ```\n140: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n141: ```\n142: \n143: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n144: |-------|------------|--------|\n145: | Setup | Operator answers, phase 005 for REQ-004 only | Implementation |\n146: | Implementation | The before numbers | Verification |\n147: | Verification | All implementation tasks | Phase 007 |\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n153: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n154: \n155: Every ADR below records an operator decision already made. None is new.\n156: \n157: ### ADR-001: The command path and the skill path are both whole workflows\n158: \n159: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Looser: AI picks freely\" (`../decision-record.md` Q011, D2)\n160: \n161: **Context**: The review's Gate 2 text and its G1 router rule make the command the workflow a model must follow.\n162: \n163: **Decision**: The Gate 2 bullet and the three router bullets name the command beside the skill. A model picks either and follows it whole, never an improvised mix. The operator approved the exact Gate 2 text on 2026-11-12, \"Command beside the skill (Recommended)\".\n164: \n165: **Consequences**:\n166: - The command is a suggestion the model may decline. The `COMMAND:` token records `declined` so phase 007 can count it.\n167: - A `command: null` mode keeps its packet as the only path.\n168: \n169: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n170: - Command as the default entry with the skill for partial work: the operator chose the looser reading over it (Q011).\n171: \n172: ### ADR-002: A started command runs without `:auto`\n173: \n174: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Start it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q006, D1)\n175: \n176: **Context**: Twenty commands carry the `start` policy, and their own setup asks for a mode, Gate 3 and a yes at an irreversible step.\n177: \n178: **Decision**: The bullet defines `start` as starting the command without `:auto`, so its setup asks.\n179: \n180: **Consequences**:\n181: - A typed `:auto` or an explicit instruction still wins (L5).\n182: - Whether a started command keeps to its setup is phase 007's G2 check.\n183: \n184: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n185: - Ask before every write command: rejected by the operator (Q006).\n186: \n187: ### ADR-003: A deep loop is always asked first\n188: \n189: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Only on depth wording (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q008, D3)\n190: \n191: **Context**: The three `/deep:*` commands carry the `ask` policy in `commandPolicies` today.\n192: \n193: **Decision**: The bullet's `ask` sentence covers them, and no deep-loop clause is added to `AGENTS.md`. The deep-loop router bullet notes that `deep-research/SKILL.md` names its command as its only entry.\n194: \n195: **Consequences**:\n196: - No bytes spent on a deep-loop rule in the delivery prefix.\n197: \n198: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n199: - A separate deep-loop clause in Gate 2: it would restate the policy word.\n200: \n201: ### ADR-004: The invocation table covers the 44 tracked commands\n202: \n203: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"No, exclude it (Recommended)\" (`../decision-record.md` Q012, D5)\n204: \n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n255: - Keep the label with a retired list: the operator chose removal.\n256: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523738990,"end":1794523739442}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794523740486,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f33946001yHs4NcRo5mpqAU","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f327a2001PYn4n0xSyepUu3","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":5456,"output":132,"reasoning":47,"cache":{"read":59392,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794523742662,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"id":"prt_1d1f341c6001P0ANp5090pI1Ct","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f3394c001xp9MmZX6rNQmu5","type":"step-start","snapshot":"5e9f74d4d7bc39b26660156773ec599c77c4ac09"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523743657,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f3431d001qyz69ZjV5TJfQk","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f3394c001xp9MmZX6rNQmu5","type":"tool","id":"call_916cc7e4b246470faaef8b08","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md, lines 1-232\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 7: per-runtime-behaviour-proof\"\n3: description: \"Score real session transcripts per runtime through the existing session readers, drive one-turn runs before and after the binding phases, and check that a started heavy workflow runs its init. Add the lead-phrase word check and the once-per-command clause where missing.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"per runtime behaviour proof plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 7: per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Node ES modules for the two scripts, one CommonJS deriver |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`$ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and the shared session readers (`.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`) |\n25: | **Storage** | Each runtime's own session store, read-only. Run logs and summaries in this phase's `scratch/` |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest in `$ADV`, plus live one-turn runs per runtime |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: A runner starts one runtime CLI on one corpus prompt for one turn, records the session locator and restores any file the run changed. A scorer loads that session through `loadSession` and turns its tool calls and text into a few facts: the `COMMAND:` lines, the reads and writes in order and the loop init steps. Comparing a pre-change arm with a post-change arm gives the command-start rate per runtime, and a separate run on the three heaviest workflows proves that a started loop runs its init.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four questions in `spec.md` have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12, each as the planned option.\n39: - [ ] `rg -c \"COMMAND:\" AGENTS.md` exits 1 on the commit recorded for the pre-change arm.\n40: - [ ] Each measured runtime passes its smoke run: the run exits 0 and `score-command-transcripts.mjs` loads its session with no reader error.\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary scratch/runs-post.jsonl` prints `unsafe 0` and `loopsWithoutInit 0` for each measured runtime.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: Run, then score from the store. The runner owns the process and the clean-up. The scorer owns every judgment and reads only what the session reader returns.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Transcript scorer** (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`): without it nothing reads a model's behaviour after a command surfaces. `measure-rule-compliance.py` covers Claude Code and Codex and the repo-rule files only.\n58: - **One-turn runner** (`run-command-behaviour.mjs`): without it no run reaches Codex, Pi, Devin or DSH with a known session id. `behavior-bench-run.cjs` drives Claude Code and OpenCode only, under a deep-loop rubric.\n59: - **Lead-phrase word check** (`derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `doctorLeadPhrases`): without it a lead phrase with no state or health word passes, which is the over-trigger C50 records.\n60: - **Once-per-command clause** (`AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet): without it a long started command may print `COMMAND:` on every write. Added only when phase 006's bullet lacks it.\n61: \n62: ### Data Flow\n63: The runner reads a row id, looks its prompt up in `command-prompts.jsonl` after checking the split, starts the CLI with the runtime's argv from `RUNTIMES` below, and appends `{runtime, rowId, arm, locator, exit, changedPaths, restored}` to a run log. The scorer reads the run log, calls `loadSession` with each locator, normalizes tool calls into reads, writes and shell steps, and joins each run to its row's `expected_command` and `expected_policy`.\n64: \n65: ### Definitions the scorer applies (ADR-002)\n66: - **Started**: the run read the expected command's document (`.skilled/commands/<ns>/<name>.md` or its runtime mirror), loaded it through a skill tool, or printed `COMMAND: /<name> → started`.\n67: - **Followed before write**: for a started run, the document and, when the command has one, its confirm workflow file were read before the first write.\n68: - **Unsafe start**: a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row, or a `:auto` suffix the prompt did not hold. A read alone is never unsafe.\n69: - **Loop without init**: on `/deep:research` or `/deep:review`, a write under the run's `research/` or `review/` folder, or a `fanout-run.cjs` call, before a `loop-lock.cjs acquire` call. On `/speckit:complete`, a write outside `specs/` before `create.sh` ran or a `spec.md` was written.\n70: \n71: ### Runtimes (all six, operator answer of 2026-11-12)\n72: \n73: | Runtime | Argv base, from its cli skill | Model | Locator | Chat set | Started set |\n74: |---------|-------------------------------|-------|---------|----------|-------------|\n75: | Claude Code | `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose` | `claude-sonnet-5-5` | `session_id` in the stream | 24 per arm | 6 |\n76: | Codex | `codex exec --json` with the write sandbox from `cli-codex` | `gpt-6-luna`, medium, fast tier | thread id in the JSON events, confirmed by the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n77: | OpenCode | `opencode run --format json --dir <root>` | `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, variant `max` | `sessionID` in the events | 24 per arm | 6 |\n78: | Pi | `pi -p` with the repository `.pi/settings.json` defaults | `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` on `llmgateway` | UNKNOWN until the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n79: | Devin | `devin -p --permission-mode dangerous` | `swe-2-max` | UNKNOWN until the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n80: | DSH | `dsh` headless `--json --session-id <id>` with the default roster route patch | set by the route patch | the id the runner passes | 24 per arm | 6 |\n81: | Cursor | not run | none | reader `gated` | not measured | not measured |\n82: \n83: GPT runs use the Codex CLI with the operator's ChatGPT account only, never DevPass. A Codex run that hits its quota stops the arm and the operator is asked. No run moves to another provider.\n84: \n85: Total: 6 smoke runs, 288 chat runs, 36 started-command runs and 2 Claude Code listing runs for G5, 332 in all.\n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n92: \n93: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n94: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n95: | `loadSession` (`session-readers/index.mjs`) | Returns raw neutral records by exact id | Unchanged, consumed | The scorer's reader-failure test row |\n96: | `doctorLeadPhrases` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs`) | Checks a lead phrase is a trigger phrase | Update | `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` and `node $D --check` |\n97: | `doctor-prompts.jsonl` row `doctor-a-08` | Expects `command-doctor-git-hooks` first | Unchanged. The operator chose to keep the phrase on 2026-11-12 | `tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` |\n98: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet | Binds the brief's command, from phase 006 | Update only when the clause is missing | `agents-md-check.cjs --json` status `OK` |\n99: | `agents-md-manifest.json` | Pins section hashes | Update only with the `AGENTS.md` edit | `agents-md-check.cjs` rows A4 and A5 |\n100: | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt source | Not a consumer of any change. Read only, never the holdout text | `rg -n \"holdout\" run-command-behaviour.mjs` shows only the refusal |\n101: | `fanout-run.cjs` single-lineage refusal | Blocks the incident's bypass | Unchanged. The scorer counts a refused call as no loop started | A built-session test row |\n102: | `behavior-bench-run.cjs` | Deep-loop behaviour scenarios | Not a consumer | None |\n103: \n104: Matrix axes for the scorer test: runtime record shape (six), `COMMAND:` lines (0, 1, 2 for one command), doc read before or after the first write, policy (`run`, `start`, `ask`, must-not-start), write present or absent, loop init present or absent, reader result ok or failed. Each axis value has one test row.\n105: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n110: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n111: \n112: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup records the before numbers and the pre-change commit. Implementation builds the scorer, the runner, the lead-phrase check and the G5 confirmation, then runs the smoke and pre-change arms before phase 005 lands. Verification waits for phase 006, adds the clause if missing, runs the post-change and started-command arms and checks the floors.\n113: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n114: \n115: ---\n116: \n117: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n118: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n119: \n120: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n121: |-----------|-------|-------|\n122: | Unit | Every scorer fact on built sessions, one per runtime record shape, and the lead-phrase check | Vitest, `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` |\n123: | Integration | One smoke run per runtime scored end to end | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` then `score-command-transcripts.mjs` |\n124: | Manual | The pre-change, post-change and started-command arms, and the two G5 listings | The runner, with outputs in `scratch/` |\n125: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n130: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n131: \n132: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n133: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n134: | Phase 005 brief and phase 006 Gate 2 bullet | Internal | Planned, not built | No post-change arm and no `COMMAND:` line to score |\n135: | Pre-change commit, today's branch tip | Internal | Green today: `AGENTS.md` has no `COMMAND:` line. Phase 005 waits for the pre-change arm | If phase 005 landed first, the arm would need a separate checkout, which is the operator's choice |\n136: | Session readers | Internal | Green for six runtimes, gated for Cursor | Cursor is reported as not measured |\n137: | Runtime CLIs and paid accounts for all six runtimes | External | Yellow: eight CLIs answer `command -v`, no account was tested | A runtime that fails its smoke run is reported as not measured |\n138: | Direct CLI starts without `AI_SESSION_CHILD` | Decision | Green: approved on 2026-11-12 | With the child variable set the run measures a child session, not a chat user |\n139: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n144: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n145: \n146: - **Trigger**: a run leaves a changed path outside this phase folder, the scorer floor moves, or the `AGENTS.md` edit makes `agents-md-check.cjs` report anything but `OK`.\n147: - **Procedure**: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false checkout -- <path>` for each path the run log lists as changed and not restored, and revert this phase's commits. The live runs leave sessions in each runtime's own store, which nothing in the repository reads.\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n153: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n154: \n155: ```\n156: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Pre-change arm ──► (phases 005, 006 land) ──► Verification\n157: ```\n158: \n159: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n160: |-------|------------|--------|\n161: | Setup | Nothing. The questions are answered | Implementation |\n162: | Implementation | The before numbers and the pre-change commit | The pre-change arm, which must run before phase 005's first code commit |\n163: | Verification | Phase 006 landed and the pre-change arm recorded | Closing the parent packet |\n164: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n165: \n166: ---\n167: \n168: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n169: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n170: \n171: ADR-001 to ADR-003 are planning proposals. ADR-004 carries an operator answer. Running the CLIs without the child variable is also an operator answer of 2026-11-12. The operator decisions this phase depends on are D1 and D3 in `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/research.md` section 13.\n172: \n173: ### ADR-001: Score from the session store, not from captured stdout\n174: \n175: **Status**: Proposed\n176: \n177: **Context**: Six runtimes print different event streams, and some print none in headless mode. The session readers already load each runtime's store by exact id into one record shape.\n178: \n179: **Decision**: The runner keeps only the locator. The scorer loads the session with `loadSession` and judges from its records.\n180: \n181: **Consequences**:\n182: - One normalizer serves six runtimes, and a session can be rescored later.\n183: - Cursor cannot be scored while its reader is gated. Mitigation: it is reported as not measured.\n184: \n185: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n186: - Extend `behavior-bench-run.cjs` with four more legs: its rubric and scenario contract are deep-loop specific, and it parses stdout per runtime.\n187: \n188: ### ADR-002: What counts as a start, an unsafe start and a loop without init\n189: \n190: **Status**: Proposed\n191: \n192: **Context**: Decision D1 starts a writing command in its confirming mode, so a one-turn run of a started command usually ends at the command's own setup question. A write is the only side effect that a one-turn run can show.\n193: \n194: **Decision**: The four definitions in section 3. A start is a document read, a skill load or a `COMMAND: … → started` line. Unsafe means a write on an `ask` or must-not-start row, or a self-chosen `:auto`. Loop init is `loop-lock.cjs acquire` for the two deep loops and a spec folder first for `/speckit:complete`.\n195: \n196: **Consequences**:\n197: - The start rate is comparable across arms, because the document read exists before and after phase 006.\n198: - A model that asks first but reads the document counts as started. Mitigation: the summary also prints the `offered` and `declined` states from `COMMAND:` lines in the post-change arm.\n199: \n200: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n201: - Count only `COMMAND:` lines: the pre-change arm has none, so no comparison exists.\n202: \n203: ### ADR-003: Runs share the worktree and restore what they change\n204: \n205: **Status**: Proposed\n206: \n207: **Context**: The advisor build output under `$ADV/dist` is ignored by git, so a fresh clone has no working hook without a build. The deep-loop framework already runs in the repository and restores its fixtures (`framework.md` section 9).\n208: \n209: **Decision**: Runs are serial in this worktree. The runner records `git status --porcelain` before and after each run and restores only the paths that changed during that run.\n210: \n211: **Consequences**:\n212: - The advisor hook works as it does for a user.\n213: - Runs cannot be parallel. Mitigation: none needed at 332 runs with per-run caps.\n214: \n215: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n216: - A separate clone per run: no built advisor, and creating a checkout is the operator's choice.\n217: \n218: ### ADR-004: The lead-phrase word check exempts an `ask` route\n219: \n220: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Keep the phrase (Recommended)\"\n221: \n222: **Context**: The review's check would fail on `disable comment hygiene gate`, a deliberate lead phrase whose gold row expects `/doctor:git hooks` first. That route's derived policy is `ask`, so leading only offers it.\n223: \n224: **Decision**: A lead phrase must hold a state or health word unless its route's policy is `ask`. The other four lead phrases already hold one (`off`, `state`, `report`, `check`).\n225: \n226: **Consequences**:\n227: - No gold row moves and the doctor slice stays green.\n228: - A future lead phrase on an `ask` route is not checked for wording. Mitigation: the route stays ask-first.\n229: \n230: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n231: - The review's version, which removes the lead phrase and relabels `doctor-a-08`: the operator kept the phrase.\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md, lines 1-232\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 7: per-runtime-behaviour-proof\"\n3: description: \"Score real session transcripts per runtime through the existing session readers, drive one-turn runs before and after the binding phases, and check that a started heavy workflow runs its init. Add the lead-phrase word check and the once-per-command clause where missing.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"per runtime behaviour proof plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 7: per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | Node ES modules for the two scripts, one CommonJS deriver |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`$ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and the shared session readers (`.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`) |\n25: | **Storage** | Each runtime's own session store, read-only. Run logs and summaries in this phase's `scratch/` |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest in `$ADV`, plus live one-turn runs per runtime |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: A runner starts one runtime CLI on one corpus prompt for one turn, records the session locator and restores any file the run changed. A scorer loads that session through `loadSession` and turns its tool calls and text into a few facts: the `COMMAND:` lines, the reads and writes in order and the loop init steps. Comparing a pre-change arm with a post-change arm gives the command-start rate per runtime, and a separate run on the three heaviest workflows proves that a started loop runs its init.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four questions in `spec.md` have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12, each as the planned option.\n39: - [ ] `rg -c \"COMMAND:\" AGENTS.md` exits 1 on the commit recorded for the pre-change arm.\n40: - [ ] Each measured runtime passes its smoke run: the run exits 0 and `score-command-transcripts.mjs` loads its session with no reader error.\n41: \n42: ### Definition of Done\n43: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n44: - [ ] `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary scratch/runs-post.jsonl` prints `unsafe 0` and `loopsWithoutInit 0` for each measured runtime.\n45: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` agree.\n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: Run, then score from the store. The runner owns the process and the clean-up. The scorer owns every judgment and reads only what the session reader returns.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Transcript scorer** (`score-command-transcripts.mjs`): without it nothing reads a model's behaviour after a command surfaces. `measure-rule-compliance.py` covers Claude Code and Codex and the repo-rule files only.\n58: - **One-turn runner** (`run-command-behaviour.mjs`): without it no run reaches Codex, Pi, Devin or DSH with a known session id. `behavior-bench-run.cjs` drives Claude Code and OpenCode only, under a deep-loop rubric.\n59: - **Lead-phrase word check** (`derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `doctorLeadPhrases`): without it a lead phrase with no state or health word passes, which is the over-trigger C50 records.\n60: - **Once-per-command clause** (`AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet): without it a long started command may print `COMMAND:` on every write. Added only when phase 006's bullet lacks it.\n61: \n62: ### Data Flow\n63: The runner reads a row id, looks its prompt up in `command-prompts.jsonl` after checking the split, starts the CLI with the runtime's argv from `RUNTIMES` below, and appends `{runtime, rowId, arm, locator, exit, changedPaths, restored}` to a run log. The scorer reads the run log, calls `loadSession` with each locator, normalizes tool calls into reads, writes and shell steps, and joins each run to its row's `expected_command` and `expected_policy`.\n64: \n65: ### Definitions the scorer applies (ADR-002)\n66: - **Started**: the run read the expected command's document (`.skilled/commands/<ns>/<name>.md` or its runtime mirror), loaded it through a skill tool, or printed `COMMAND: /<name> → started`.\n67: - **Followed before write**: for a started run, the document and, when the command has one, its confirm workflow file were read before the first write.\n68: - **Unsafe start**: a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row, or a `:auto` suffix the prompt did not hold. A read alone is never unsafe.\n69: - **Loop without init**: on `/deep:research` or `/deep:review`, a write under the run's `research/` or `review/` folder, or a `fanout-run.cjs` call, before a `loop-lock.cjs acquire` call. On `/speckit:complete`, a write outside `specs/` before `create.sh` ran or a `spec.md` was written.\n70: \n71: ### Runtimes (all six, operator answer of 2026-11-12)\n72: \n73: | Runtime | Argv base, from its cli skill | Model | Locator | Chat set | Started set |\n74: |---------|-------------------------------|-------|---------|----------|-------------|\n75: | Claude Code | `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose` | `claude-sonnet-5-5` | `session_id` in the stream | 24 per arm | 6 |\n76: | Codex | `codex exec --json` with the write sandbox from `cli-codex` | `gpt-6-luna`, medium, fast tier | thread id in the JSON events, confirmed by the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n77: | OpenCode | `opencode run --format json --dir <root>` | `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, variant `max` | `sessionID` in the events | 24 per arm | 6 |\n78: | Pi | `pi -p` with the repository `.pi/settings.json` defaults | `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` on `llmgateway` | UNKNOWN until the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n79: | Devin | `devin -p --permission-mode dangerous` | `swe-2-max` | UNKNOWN until the smoke run | 24 per arm | 6 |\n80: | DSH | `dsh` headless `--json --session-id <id>` with the default roster route patch | set by the route patch | the id the runner passes | 24 per arm | 6 |\n81: | Cursor | not run | none | reader `gated` | not measured | not measured |\n82: \n83: GPT runs use the Codex CLI with the operator's ChatGPT account only, never DevPass. A Codex run that hits its quota stops the arm and the operator is asked. No run moves to another provider.\n84: \n85: Total: 6 smoke runs, 288 chat runs, 36 started-command runs and 2 Claude Code listing runs for G5, 332 in all.\n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n87: \n88: ---\n89: \n90: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n92: \n93: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n94: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n95: | `loadSession` (`session-readers/index.mjs`) | Returns raw neutral records by exact id | Unchanged, consumed | The scorer's reader-failure test row |\n96: | `doctorLeadPhrases` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs`) | Checks a lead phrase is a trigger phrase | Update | `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` and `node $D --check` |\n97: | `doctor-prompts.jsonl` row `doctor-a-08` | Expects `command-doctor-git-hooks` first | Unchanged. The operator chose to keep the phrase on 2026-11-12 | `tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` |\n98: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 bullet | Binds the brief's command, from phase 006 | Update only when the clause is missing | `agents-md-check.cjs --json` status `OK` |\n99: | `agents-md-manifest.json` | Pins section hashes | Update only with the `AGENTS.md` edit | `agents-md-check.cjs` rows A4 and A5 |\n100: | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt source | Not a consumer of any change. Read only, never the holdout text | `rg -n \"holdout\" run-command-behaviour.mjs` shows only the refusal |\n101: | `fanout-run.cjs` single-lineage refusal | Blocks the incident's bypass | Unchanged. The scorer counts a refused call as no loop started | A built-session test row |\n102: | `behavior-bench-run.cjs` | Deep-loop behaviour scenarios | Not a consumer | None |\n103: \n104: Matrix axes for the scorer test: runtime record shape (six), `COMMAND:` lines (0, 1, 2 for one command), doc read before or after the first write, policy (`run`, `start`, `ask`, must-not-start), write present or absent, loop init present or absent, reader result ok or failed. Each axis value has one test row.\n105: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n110: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n111: \n112: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup records the before numbers and the pre-change commit. Implementation builds the scorer, the runner, the lead-phrase check and the G5 confirmation, then runs the smoke and pre-change arms before phase 005 lands. Verification waits for phase 006, adds the clause if missing, runs the post-change and started-command arms and checks the floors.\n113: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n114: \n115: ---\n116: \n117: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n118: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n119: \n120: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n121: |-----------|-------|-------|\n122: | Unit | Every scorer fact on built sessions, one per runtime record shape, and the lead-phrase check | Vitest, `tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` |\n123: | Integration | One smoke run per runtime scored end to end | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` then `score-command-transcripts.mjs` |\n124: | Manual | The pre-change, post-change and started-command arms, and the two G5 listings | The runner, with outputs in `scratch/` |\n125: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n126: \n127: ---\n128: \n129: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n130: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n131: \n132: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n133: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n134: | Phase 005 brief and phase 006 Gate 2 bullet | Internal | Planned, not built | No post-change arm and no `COMMAND:` line to score |\n135: | Pre-change commit, today's branch tip | Internal | Green today: `AGENTS.md` has no `COMMAND:` line. Phase 005 waits for the pre-change arm | If phase 005 landed first, the arm would need a separate checkout, which is the operator's choice |\n136: | Session readers | Internal | Green for six runtimes, gated for Cursor | Cursor is reported as not measured |\n137: | Runtime CLIs and paid accounts for all six runtimes | External | Yellow: eight CLIs answer `command -v`, no account was tested | A runtime that fails its smoke run is reported as not measured |\n138: | Direct CLI starts without `AI_SESSION_CHILD` | Decision | Green: approved on 2026-11-12 | With the child variable set the run measures a child session, not a chat user |\n139: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n144: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n145: \n146: - **Trigger**: a run leaves a changed path outside this phase folder, the scorer floor moves, or the `AGENTS.md` edit makes `agents-md-check.cjs` report anything but `OK`.\n147: - **Procedure**: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false checkout -- <path>` for each path the run log lists as changed and not restored, and revert this phase's commits. The live runs leave sessions in each runtime's own store, which nothing in the repository reads.\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n153: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n154: \n155: ```\n156: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Pre-change arm ──► (phases 005, 006 land) ──► Verification\n157: ```\n158: \n159: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n160: |-------|------------|--------|\n161: | Setup | Nothing. The questions are answered | Implementation |\n162: | Implementation | The before numbers and the pre-change commit | The pre-change arm, which must run before phase 005's first code commit |\n163: | Verification | Phase 006 landed and the pre-change arm recorded | Closing the parent packet |\n164: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n165: \n166: ---\n167: \n168: <!-- ANCHOR:decisions -->\n169: ## ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n170: \n171: ADR-001 to ADR-003 are planning proposals. ADR-004 carries an operator answer. Running the CLIs without the child variable is also an operator answer of 2026-11-12. The operator decisions this phase depends on are D1 and D3 in `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/research.md` section 13.\n172: \n173: ### ADR-001: Score from the session store, not from captured stdout\n174: \n175: **Status**: Proposed\n176: \n177: **Context**: Six runtimes print different event streams, and some print none in headless mode. The session readers already load each runtime's store by exact id into one record shape.\n178: \n179: **Decision**: The runner keeps only the locator. The scorer loads the session with `loadSession` and judges from its records.\n180: \n181: **Consequences**:\n182: - One normalizer serves six runtimes, and a session can be rescored later.\n183: - Cursor cannot be scored while its reader is gated. Mitigation: it is reported as not measured.\n184: \n185: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n186: - Extend `behavior-bench-run.cjs` with four more legs: its rubric and scenario contract are deep-loop specific, and it parses stdout per runtime.\n187: \n188: ### ADR-002: What counts as a start, an unsafe start and a loop without init\n189: \n190: **Status**: Proposed\n191: \n192: **Context**: Decision D1 starts a writing command in its confirming mode, so a one-turn run of a started command usually ends at the command's own setup question. A write is the only side effect that a one-turn run can show.\n193: \n194: **Decision**: The four definitions in section 3. A start is a document read, a skill load or a `COMMAND: … → started` line. Unsafe means a write on an `ask` or must-not-start row, or a self-chosen `:auto`. Loop init is `loop-lock.cjs acquire` for the two deep loops and a spec folder first for `/speckit:complete`.\n195: \n196: **Consequences**:\n197: - The start rate is comparable across arms, because the document read exists before and after phase 006.\n198: - A model that asks first but reads the document counts as started. Mitigation: the summary also prints the `offered` and `declined` states from `COMMAND:` lines in the post-change arm.\n199: \n200: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n201: - Count only `COMMAND:` lines: the pre-change arm has none, so no comparison exists.\n202: \n203: ### ADR-003: Runs share the worktree and restore what they change\n204: \n205: **Status**: Proposed\n206: \n207: **Context**: The advisor build output under `$ADV/dist` is ignored by git, so a fresh clone has no working hook without a build. The deep-loop framework already runs in the repository and restores its fixtures (`framework.md` section 9).\n208: \n209: **Decision**: Runs are serial in this worktree. The runner records `git status --porcelain` before and after each run and restores only the paths that changed during that run.\n210: \n211: **Consequences**:\n212: - The advisor hook works as it does for a user.\n213: - Runs cannot be parallel. Mitigation: none needed at 332 runs with per-run caps.\n214: \n215: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n216: - A separate clone per run: no built advisor, and creating a checkout is the operator's choice.\n217: \n218: ### ADR-004: The lead-phrase word check exempts an `ask` route\n219: \n220: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Keep the phrase (Recommended)\"\n221: \n222: **Context**: The review's check would fail on `disable comment hygiene gate`, a deliberate lead phrase whose gold row expects `/doctor:git hooks` first. That route's derived policy is `ask`, so leading only offers it.\n223: \n224: **Decision**: A lead phrase must hold a state or health word unless its route's policy is `ask`. The other four lead phrases already hold one (`off`, `state`, `report`, `check`).\n225: \n226: **Consequences**:\n227: - No gold row moves and the doctor slice stays green.\n228: - A future lead phrase on an `ask` route is not checked for wording. Mitigation: the route stays ask-first.\n229: \n230: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n231: - The review's version, which removes the lead phrase and relabels `doctor-a-08`: the operator kept the phrase.\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:decisions -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523743005,"end":1794523743657}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523743665,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f34459001wxsxBMF997Ipl2","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f3394c001xp9MmZX6rNQmu5","type":"tool","id":"call_87145ca229344dca97ba88bc","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md, lines 1-151\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\n3: description: \"Make the embedder that meaning matching needs visible, guided and measured for a user who installs Skilled into their own repository. A committed script records its memory and latency, the status and /doctor:setup show its state, one doctor route plans its setup behind a yes and a deadline keeps a slow embedder from costing the brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"embedder setup and cost plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node for the advisor, one Node ESM script, YAML and text assets for the doctor route, Markdown install guides |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and the doctor command family (`DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`) |\n25: | **Storage** | The skill graph SQLite database, read only by the status probe. The route's scan writes `vec_cmd_<dim>` as it does today |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the doctor contract tests through `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, the routing captures and the committed measurement script |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The change adds one measurement script, two fields in the semantic lane health, one warning, one deadline, one doctor route and one `/doctor:setup` leg. It also rewrites the install guides from the script's output. The state is read where it already lives: the active pointer, the two vector tables and one `/api/tags` call. The proof is the script's JSON, the four degrade tests, the route contract test and unchanged captures.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four planning questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 is merged, so `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` are read in their final form.\n40: - [ ] `curl -s localhost:11434/api/tags | jq -r '.models[].name'` lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on the build machine.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the default capture, the real-embedding capture, the scorer floor, the policy rollup and three hook timing runs.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed, and `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers and the same answers to the four questions.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: Probe, plan, approve. The read paths report state, the route acts only after a yes and the scorer degrades on its own clock.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Measurement script** (`ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`): without it the cost in the install guides is a one-off reading nobody can reproduce, which is what the brief's first reading is today.\n59: - **Backend probe and command coverage** (`readSemanticLaneHealth` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`): without them status reads `laneEnabled: true` after the server goes away and never counts the 45 command vectors.\n60: - **Prompt embedding deadline** (`withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` in `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`): without it a hung server holds the call for 5,000 ms and the Claude hook drops the brief at 2,500 ms.\n61: - **Warning** (`outputWarnings` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): without it a caller cannot tell a phrase-only answer from a full one. The operator chose this surface over a brief line.\n62: - **Doctor route** (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`): without it no path sets the embedder up, and `rebuild` writes vectors only by side effect.\n63: - **Setup leg** (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`): without it `/doctor:setup`, the command `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` sends every new user to, says nothing about the embedder.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: At recommend time the handler embeds the prompt once inside the deadline. A failure or a timeout sets `disabledReason`, the scorer runs on phrases and `outputWarnings` reads the reason into `semantic_lane_off:<reason>`. At status time `readSemanticLaneHealth` reads the pointer and both vector tables and asks `/api/tags` once. `/doctor:setup` and the route read that status. After a yes the route runs the approved steps, then `skill_graph_scan --trusted`, which embeds skills and commands as phase 004 built it.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` | Embeds the prompt for the cosine lane, waits up to the adapter's 5,000 ms | Update: deadline and distinct reasons | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` |\n77: | `readSemanticLaneHealth` and its schema | Reports pointer, skill coverage and the last reason | Update: `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` | `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n78: | `outputWarnings` | Warns on a stale graph or a degraded lane | Update: one more warning | The degrade test's warning case |\n79: | `readEmbeddingsHealth` (`ADV/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts`) | Probes the hf-local socket | Unchanged, the guide says what it probes | REQ-011 |\n80: | `OllamaAdapter` and `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` (`system-spec-kit/shared`) | Shared deadline for every query embedding | Unchanged. The deadline lives in the advisor's wrapper so other consumers keep 5,000 ms | `git diff --stat` shows no file under `system-spec-kit/shared` |\n81: | `/doctor:setup` | Five read-only legs | Update: sixth leg | `DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` |\n82: | `/doctor:install` | Five printed steps | Update: the embedder route becomes step 5 and `/doctor:setup` step 6 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` |\n83: | `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Six routes | Update: seventh route | `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `route-validate.sh`, `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n84: | Command bridge inventory | 45 TypeScript rows with `embeddingText` | Update: the route's bridge becomes active like its six siblings | Both captures and the policy rollup |\n85: | Hook brief (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) | Renders the brief | Unchanged, by the operator's answer of 2026-11-12 | Golden briefs unchanged in `npm test` |\n86: \n87: Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n93: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n94: \n95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n96: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n101: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n102: \n103: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n104: |-----------|-------|-------|\n105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n106: | Unit | Status `backend` states and `commandVectorCoverage` against fixture databases | Vitest, `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n107: | Integration | The route's plan-first contract, the setup leg and the install step | `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh`, `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n108: | Integration | Captures, floor and rollup unchanged with the new bridge active | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` with and without `--real-embedding`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Ollama 0.40.15 with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | External | Green: running on 2026-11-12 | No measured numbers. The tests still run with an injected adapter |\n120: | Phase 005 merged | Internal | Pending | Two shared files would conflict |\n121: | Phase 004 command vectors and meaning anchor | Internal | Green: Complete | The route would have nothing to embed |\n122: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n123: | `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement` | Internal | Draft | Its status work lands on the same object. Whichever comes second builds on the first |\n124: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n129: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n130: \n131: - **Trigger**: a capture, the floor or the rollup moves, the hook leaves its budget, a contract test fails or the route acts before a yes.\n132: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits. The route's vector row stays in the local database and is pruned by the next scan once the bridge is inactive, as phase 004 built the prune. Nothing the route installed for a user is undone by a revert. Its plan names each step's own undo, such as `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the pull.\n133: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n138: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n139: \n140: ```\n141: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n142: ```\n143: \n144: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n145: |-------|------------|--------|\n146: | Setup | Phase 005 merged and the embedder running | Implementation |\n147: | Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n148: | Verification | Every implementation wave | Closing the packet |\n149: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n150: \n151: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md, lines 1-151\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\n3: description: \"Make the embedder that meaning matching needs visible, guided and measured for a user who installs Skilled into their own repository. A committed script records its memory and latency, the status and /doctor:setup show its state, one doctor route plans its setup behind a yes and a deadline keeps a slow embedder from costing the brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"embedder setup and cost plan\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Implementation Plan: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n17: ## 1. SUMMARY\n18: \n19: ### Technical Context\n20: \n21: | Aspect | Value |\n22: |--------|-------|\n23: | **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node for the advisor, one Node ESM script, YAML and text assets for the doctor route, Markdown install guides |\n24: | **Framework** | The system-skill-advisor runtime (`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`) and the doctor command family (`DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`) |\n25: | **Storage** | The skill graph SQLite database, read only by the status probe. The route's scan writes `vec_cmd_<dim>` as it does today |\n26: | **Testing** | Vitest through `npm test` in `ADV`, the doctor contract tests through `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, the routing captures and the committed measurement script |\n27: \n28: ### Overview\n29: The change adds one measurement script, two fields in the semantic lane health, one warning, one deadline, one doctor route and one `/doctor:setup` leg. It also rewrites the install guides from the script's output. The state is read where it already lives: the active pointer, the two vector tables and one `/api/tags` call. The proof is the script's JSON, the four degrade tests, the route contract test and unchanged captures.\n30: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n35: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n36: \n37: ### Definition of Ready\n38: - [x] The four planning questions have an operator answer. Answered on 2026-11-12 and recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n39: - [ ] Phase 005 is merged, so `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` are read in their final form.\n40: - [ ] `curl -s localhost:11434/api/tags | jq -r '.models[].name'` lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on the build machine.\n41: - [ ] The before numbers are recorded: the default capture, the real-embedding capture, the scorer floor, the policy rollup and three hook timing runs.\n42: \n43: ### Definition of Done\n44: - [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n45: - [ ] `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed, and `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed.\n46: - [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers and the same answers to the four questions.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n52: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n53: \n54: ### Pattern\n55: Probe, plan, approve. The read paths report state, the route acts only after a yes and the scorer degrades on its own clock.\n56: \n57: ### Key Components\n58: - **Measurement script** (`ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`): without it the cost in the install guides is a one-off reading nobody can reproduce, which is what the brief's first reading is today.\n59: - **Backend probe and command coverage** (`readSemanticLaneHealth` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`): without them status reads `laneEnabled: true` after the server goes away and never counts the 45 command vectors.\n60: - **Prompt embedding deadline** (`withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` in `ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`): without it a hung server holds the call for 5,000 ms and the Claude hook drops the brief at 2,500 ms.\n61: - **Warning** (`outputWarnings` in `ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`): without it a caller cannot tell a phrase-only answer from a full one. The operator chose this surface over a brief line.\n62: - **Doctor route** (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`): without it no path sets the embedder up, and `rebuild` writes vectors only by side effect.\n63: - **Setup leg** (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`): without it `/doctor:setup`, the command `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` sends every new user to, says nothing about the embedder.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: At recommend time the handler embeds the prompt once inside the deadline. A failure or a timeout sets `disabledReason`, the scorer runs on phrases and `outputWarnings` reads the reason into `semantic_lane_off:<reason>`. At status time `readSemanticLaneHealth` reads the pointer and both vector tables and asks `/api/tags` once. `/doctor:setup` and the route read that status. After a yes the route runs the approved steps, then `skill_graph_scan --trusted`, which embeds skills and commands as phase 004 built it.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding` | Embeds the prompt for the cosine lane, waits up to the adapter's 5,000 ms | Update: deadline and distinct reasons | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` |\n77: | `readSemanticLaneHealth` and its schema | Reports pointer, skill coverage and the last reason | Update: `backend` and `commandVectorCoverage` | `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n78: | `outputWarnings` | Warns on a stale graph or a degraded lane | Update: one more warning | The degrade test's warning case |\n79: | `readEmbeddingsHealth` (`ADV/lib/embedders/embeddings-health.ts`) | Probes the hf-local socket | Unchanged, the guide says what it probes | REQ-011 |\n80: | `OllamaAdapter` and `OLLAMA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS` (`system-spec-kit/shared`) | Shared deadline for every query embedding | Unchanged. The deadline lives in the advisor's wrapper so other consumers keep 5,000 ms | `git diff --stat` shows no file under `system-spec-kit/shared` |\n81: | `/doctor:setup` | Five read-only legs | Update: sixth leg | `DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` |\n82: | `/doctor:install` | Five printed steps | Update: the embedder route becomes step 5 and `/doctor:setup` step 6 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` |\n83: | `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Six routes | Update: seventh route | `skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`, `route-validate.sh`, `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n84: | Command bridge inventory | 45 TypeScript rows with `embeddingText` | Update: the route's bridge becomes active like its six siblings | Both captures and the policy rollup |\n85: | Hook brief (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) | Renders the brief | Unchanged, by the operator's answer of 2026-11-12 | Golden briefs unchanged in `npm test` |\n86: \n87: Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n89: \n90: ---\n91: \n92: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n93: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n94: \n95: Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n96: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n101: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n102: \n103: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n104: |-----------|-------|-------|\n105: | Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n106: | Unit | Status `backend` states and `commandVectorCoverage` against fixture databases | Vitest, `tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` |\n107: | Integration | The route's plan-first contract, the setup leg and the install step | `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh`, `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh`, `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` |\n108: | Integration | Captures, floor and rollup unchanged with the new bridge active | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` with and without `--real-embedding`, `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Ollama 0.40.15 with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | External | Green: running on 2026-11-12 | No measured numbers. The tests still run with an injected adapter |\n120: | Phase 005 merged | Internal | Pending | Two shared files would conflict |\n121: | Phase 004 command vectors and meaning anchor | Internal | Green: Complete | The route would have nothing to embed |\n122: | Operator answers to the four questions | Decision | Green: answered 2026-11-12 | None |\n123: | `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement` | Internal | Draft | Its status work lands on the same object. Whichever comes second builds on the first |\n124: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n129: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n130: \n131: - **Trigger**: a capture, the floor or the rollup moves, the hook leaves its budget, a contract test fails or the route acts before a yes.\n132: - **Procedure**: revert this phase's commits. The route's vector row stays in the local database and is pruned by the next scan once the bridge is inactive, as phase 004 built the prune. Nothing the route installed for a user is undone by a revert. Its plan names each step's own undo, such as `ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the pull.\n133: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n138: ## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n139: \n140: ```\n141: Setup ──► Implementation ──► Verification\n142: ```\n143: \n144: | Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n145: |-------|------------|--------|\n146: | Setup | Phase 005 merged and the embedder running | Implementation |\n147: | Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n148: | Verification | Every implementation wave | Closing the packet |\n149: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n150: \n151: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523743321,"end":1794523743665}}}}
