{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523868651,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f52994001xaUTsHw50oxlZg","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f51802001SNlBXNgcVRuhlH","type":"tool","id":"call_82b314cd9d394ae89ab3351e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && rg -n -i \"hook (latency|timing|time)|medianMs|p95\" 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/before.txt 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/*.txt 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"output":"008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:84:{\"case\":\"warm\",\"n\":30,\"medianMs\":6.57,\"p95Ms\":10.99,\"maxMs\":29.14}\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:109:$ for f in 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json; do echo \"$f $(jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]' $f)\"; done\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:134:- A warm query embedding takes a median of 6.57 ms and a p95 of 10.99 ms over 30 calls. One advisor CLI call takes 62.7 to 71.3 ms warm. The phase 004 hook timing moved from a middle median of 199.16 ms to 205.09 ms and a middle p95 of 231.35 ms to 261.92 ms.\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:223:| REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:237:| REQ-010 | The Claude hook over the 44 tune prompts stays inside the phase 004 budget of +25 ms median and +40 ms p95 against a same-session baseline, each the middle of three runs. |\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12:{\"case\":\"warm\",\"n\":30,\"medianMs\":6.57,\"p95Ms\":10.99,\"maxMs\":29.14}\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:39:$ for f in 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json; do echo \"$f $(jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]' $f)\"; done\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:84:{\"case\":\"warm\",\"n\":30,\"medianMs\":6.57,\"p95Ms\":10.99,\"maxMs\":29.14}\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:109:$ for f in 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json; do echo \"$f $(jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]' $f)\"; done\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:134:- A warm query embedding takes a median of 6.57 ms and a p95 of 10.99 ms over 30 calls. One advisor CLI call takes 62.7 to 71.3 ms warm. The phase 004 hook timing moved from a middle median of 199.16 ms to 205.09 ms and a middle p95 of 231.35 ms to 261.92 ms.\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:223:| REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:237:| REQ-010 | The Claude hook over the 44 tune prompts stays inside the phase 004 budget of +25 ms median and +40 ms p95 against a same-session baseline, each the middle of three runs. |\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12:{\"case\":\"warm\",\"n\":30,\"medianMs\":6.57,\"p95Ms\":10.99,\"maxMs\":29.14}\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:39:$ for f in 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json; do echo \"$f $(jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]' $f)\"; done\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && rg -n -i \\\"hook (latency|timing|time)|medianMs|p95\\\" 005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/before.txt 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/*.txt 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md 2>/dev/null | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523867540,"end":1794523868651}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794523868749,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f527330016xakg6G55hi250","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f51802001SNlBXNgcVRuhlH","type":"tool","id":"call_0054436befe0467d961ce1a8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && rg -n -i \"cold\" --glob '*.md' --glob '*.txt' --glob '*.json' . | grep -v \"holdout\" | head -30"},"output":"./007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/spec.md:61:Every check this build has so far reads the advisor's output, never the model's behaviour. A recorded session started `/deep:research` from chat, read 420 of 2,539 workflow lines and called the runner itself, so `phase_init` never ran (`specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review/001-research-egm-checks-and-chat-path-gaps/scratch/incident-chat-started-loop.md`). Decision D1 lets a model start a writing command, and research.md section 13 makes D1 depend on the check that a started command is followed. Nothing measures that today on any runtime.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:3:description: \"Meaning matching needs a local Ollama server with nomic-embed-text, yet no install document, doctor route or brief tells a user who installs Skilled into their own repository that it exists, what it costs or that it is off. This phase makes the state visible, adds one doctor route that plans the setup and waits for a yes, writes the cost into the install documents from a committed measurement script and defines the absent, cold and slow cases with tests.\"\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:32:| **Handoff Criteria** | `/doctor:setup` names the embedder state, `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` plans the setup and writes nothing without a yes, the install documents state the measured cost and the absent, model-missing, cold and slow tests pass |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:42:**Scope Boundary**: What a person who installs Skilled into their own repository sees and does about the embedder that meaning matching needs. The state, one doctor route, the install documents, a committed measurement script and the behaviour when the embedder is absent, missing its model, cold or slow. Scoring, the meaning bar, the lane weight and the embedder choice stay as they are.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:53:- A deadline on the prompt embedding and tests for the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:65:A user who installs Skilled can see whether meaning matching is on, set it up through one doctor route that shows its cost before it acts, read that cost in the install documents and keep a working advisor when the embedder is absent, cold or slow.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:130:The operator's own first reading on the same Mac, reported in the dispatch brief and not rerun here because it needs the model unloaded: `ollama serve` idle at 46 MB resident, 421 MB in total with the model loaded, cold embedding calls of 271 to 277 ms over 3 calls and one advisor CLI call of 413 ms with the model cold. The phase replaces this reading with the output of the committed script (REQ-001).\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:157:- **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:170:- Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:174:- Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:209:| `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:223:| REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:227:| REQ-005 | The prompt embedding gives up after `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS`, set to 750 ms. For an absent server, a missing model and a call past the deadline the recommendation equals the recommendation with no embedder, no error reaches the caller and `disabledReason` reads `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` or `prompt_embedding_timeout`. A cold call that answers inside the deadline is scored with its cosine. One test covers each of the four cases. |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:262:| Dependency | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on the build machine | No warm, cold or real-embedding numbers | The script exits 2 and names the server. The degrade tests inject the adapter and need no server |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:264:| Risk | A deadline too short drops a cold load on a slow machine | Med: one prompt per idle period loses meaning matching | The cold case test and the 750 ms the operator chose. The load continues on the server, which is not confirmed and is checked in T003 |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:308:| Research | 8/20 | The timeouts, the reasons and the doctor surfaces are read. The cold-load behaviour after a deadline is not |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:324:- What deadline does the prompt embedding get? Decision: \"750 ms (Recommended)\". It holds a cold call of 271 to 277 ms and stays inside the 2,500 ms hook budget.\n./spec.md:123:| 8 | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/ | The embedder for external repositories: visible state, a plan-first doctor route, the measured memory and latency cost in the install guides and defined absent, cold and slow behaviour (operator requirement, 2026-11-12) | Pending |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:87:Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:95:Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:105:| Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:147:| Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/implementation-summary.md:99:1. **The cold and idle numbers are not yet measured here.** They need the model unloaded, which the planning run did not cause. The operator's first reading stands in until T033 runs the committed script after the 5 minute unload.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given Ollama running, When `E` runs once with the model loaded and once after it unloaded on its own, Then it prints the version, model size, serve and runner memory, loaded size and expiry, warm median and p95 over 30 calls, the CLI median over 5 calls and a cold first call and writes nothing. With the server unreachable it exits 2 naming the server | `node $E > scratch/cost-warm.json`, `node $E > scratch/cost-cold.json`, `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E; echo $?` prints 2, and `git status --short` unchanged after each run | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given an injected adapter, When it answers warm, answers cold inside the deadline, is absent, lacks the model or never answers, Then the first two score with a cosine, the others return the no-embedder result inside the deadline plus 100 ms with reasons `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` and `prompt_embedding_timeout` | `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 7 passed | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:61:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `/doctor:install` and the install guides, When a user runs or reads them, Then the checklist prints the embedder route as step 5 before `/doctor:setup` as step 6, and both guides say the install sets up meaning matching by default behind a yes, give the measured cost with its date and say a no keeps a phrase-only install | `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0, `rg -n \"meaning matching\\|skill-advisor embedder\\|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` and each cost number found in `scratch/cost-warm.json` or `scratch/cost-cold.json` | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/goal.md:61:- [ ] A committed measurement script prints idle and loaded memory, warm and cold embedding latency and hook timing, and the install guide quotes its output.\n./009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/steer.md:3:Angle: performance and cost. Hook wall time (cold and warm), daemon vs no-daemon paths, embedder cost and cold start (use measure-embedder-cost.mjs and the measured-2026-11-12.txt file), token cost of the brief per prompt and per session, caching and precompute opportunities. Measure with commands that are read-only and do not start/stop ollama; report baseline and expected delta.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md:49:- [ ] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md:64:- [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/spec.md:61:Every check this build has so far reads the advisor's output, never the model's behaviour. A recorded session started `/deep:research` from chat, read 420 of 2,539 workflow lines and called the runner itself, so `phase_init` never ran (`specs/system-speckit/spec-authoring-and-continuity/005-goldfish-cold-read-plan-review/001-research-egm-checks-and-chat-path-gaps/scratch/incident-chat-started-loop.md`). Decision D1 lets a model start a writing command, and research.md section 13 makes D1 depend on the check that a started command is followed. Nothing measures that today on any runtime.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:3:description: \"Meaning matching needs a local Ollama server with nomic-embed-text, yet no install document, doctor route or brief tells a user who installs Skilled into their own repository that it exists, what it costs or that it is off. This phase makes the state visible, adds one doctor route that plans the setup and waits for a yes, writes the cost into the install documents from a committed measurement script and defines the absent, cold and slow cases with tests.\"\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:32:| **Handoff Criteria** | `/doctor:setup` names the embedder state, `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` plans the setup and writes nothing without a yes, the install documents state the measured cost and the absent, model-missing, cold and slow tests pass |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:42:**Scope Boundary**: What a person who installs Skilled into their own repository sees and does about the embedder that meaning matching needs. The state, one doctor route, the install documents, a committed measurement script and the behaviour when the embedder is absent, missing its model, cold or slow. Scoring, the meaning bar, the lane weight and the embedder choice stay as they are.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:53:- A deadline on the prompt embedding and tests for the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:65:A user who installs Skilled can see whether meaning matching is on, set it up through one doctor route that shows its cost before it acts, read that cost in the install documents and keep a working advisor when the embedder is absent, cold or slow.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:130:The operator's own first reading on the same Mac, reported in the dispatch brief and not rerun here because it needs the model unloaded: `ollama serve` idle at 46 MB resident, 421 MB in total with the model loaded, cold embedding calls of 271 to 277 ms over 3 calls and one advisor CLI call of 413 ms with the model cold. The phase replaces this reading with the output of the committed script (REQ-001).\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:157:- **Model cold.** Nothing preloads the model. The first prompt after 5 idle minutes pays the load inside the 5,000 ms query deadline.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:170:- Commit `ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`, which records the model size, the resident memory of the server and its model runner, the loaded size, the keep-alive expiry, warm and cold embedding latency and advisor CLI latency as one JSON object. Without it no number in an install document can be reproduced.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:174:- Bound the prompt embedding with its own deadline of 750 ms, give a missing model and a timeout their own `disabledReason`, add a `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` warning to a recommendation that ran without a prompt vector and test the absent, model-missing, cold and slow cases.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:209:| `ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` | Create | Absent, model-missing, cold, slow and warning cases |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:223:| REQ-001 | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` prints one JSON object with the Ollama version, the model's size on disk, the resident memory of `ollama serve` and of its model runner, the loaded size and expiry from `/api/ps`, the median and p95 of 30 warm query embeddings, the median of 5 advisor CLI calls with distinct prompts and a cold sample taken only when `/api/ps` lists no loaded model. It writes, starts and unloads nothing. It exits 2 with a message naming the server when the server does not answer. |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:227:| REQ-005 | The prompt embedding gives up after `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS`, set to 750 ms. For an absent server, a missing model and a call past the deadline the recommendation equals the recommendation with no embedder, no error reaches the caller and `disabledReason` reads `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` or `prompt_embedding_timeout`. A cold call that answers inside the deadline is scored with its cosine. One test covers each of the four cases. |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:262:| Dependency | Ollama with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` on the build machine | No warm, cold or real-embedding numbers | The script exits 2 and names the server. The degrade tests inject the adapter and need no server |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:264:| Risk | A deadline too short drops a cold load on a slow machine | Med: one prompt per idle period loses meaning matching | The cold case test and the 750 ms the operator chose. The load continues on the server, which is not confirmed and is checked in T003 |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:308:| Research | 8/20 | The timeouts, the reasons and the doctor surfaces are read. The cold-load behaviour after a deadline is not |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:324:- What deadline does the prompt embedding get? Decision: \"750 ms (Recommended)\". It holds a cold call of 271 to 277 ms and stays inside the 2,500 ms hook budget.\n./spec.md:123:| 8 | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost/ | The embedder for external repositories: visible state, a plan-first doctor route, the measured memory and latency cost in the install guides and defined absent, cold and slow behaviour (operator requirement, 2026-11-12) | Pending |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:87:Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:95:Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:105:| Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:147:| Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/implementation-summary.md:99:1. **The cold and idle numbers are not yet measured here.** They need the model unloaded, which the planning run did not cause. The operator's first reading stands in until T033 runs the committed script after the 5 minute unload.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given Ollama running, When `E` runs once with the model loaded and once after it unloaded on its own, Then it prints the version, model size, serve and runner memory, loaded size and expiry, warm median and p95 over 30 calls, the CLI median over 5 calls and a cold first call and writes nothing. With the server unreachable it exits 2 naming the server | `node $E > scratch/cost-warm.json`, `node $E > scratch/cost-cold.json`, `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E; echo $?` prints 2, and `git status --short` unchanged after each run | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given an injected adapter, When it answers warm, answers cold inside the deadline, is absent, lacks the model or never answers, Then the first two score with a cosine, the others return the no-embedder result inside the deadline plus 100 ms with reasons `prompt_embedding_unreachable`, `prompt_embedding_model_missing` and `prompt_embedding_timeout` | `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 7 passed | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/acceptance-criteria.md:61:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `/doctor:install` and the install guides, When a user runs or reads them, Then the checklist prints the embedder route as step 5 before `/doctor:setup` as step 6, and both guides say the install sets up meaning matching by default behind a yes, give the measured cost with its date and say a no keeps a phrase-only install | `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0, `rg -n \"meaning matching\\|skill-advisor embedder\\|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` and each cost number found in `scratch/cost-warm.json` or `scratch/cost-cold.json` | Unmet | - |\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/goal.md:61:- [ ] A committed measurement script prints idle and loaded memory, warm and cold embedding latency and hook timing, and the install guide quotes its output.\n./009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/steer.md:3:Angle: performance and cost. Hook wall time (cold and warm), daemon vs no-daemon paths, embedder cost and cold start (use measure-embedder-cost.mjs and the measured-2026-11-12.txt file), token cost of the brief per prompt and per session, caching and precompute opportunities. Measure with commands that are read-only and do not start/stop ollama; report baseline and expected delta.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md:49:- [ ] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n./008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md:64:- [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && rg -n -i \\\"cold\\\" --glob '*.md' --glob '*.txt' --glob '*.json' . | grep -v \\\"holdout\\\" | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794523866931,"end":1794523868749}}}}
