{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524016265,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f76c9e001zUY02GqMDkHPg2","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f74cb1001TFaYpUS3hNXohG","type":"tool","id":"call_b379d8bf7fe14051b2386c93","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers && rg -n -A6 \"Command in the brief\" spec.md plan.md tasks.md | head -40"},"output":"tasks.md:54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\ntasks.md:55:- [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\ntasks.md-56-- [ ] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on only when the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\ntasks.md-57-- [ ] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\ntasks.md-58-- [ ] T007 [P] In the observability test, change 