-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\ntasks.md-73-- [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n--\ntasks.md:76:- [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\ntasks.md-77-- [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\ntasks.md-78-<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\ntasks.md-79-\ntasks.md-80----\ntasks.md-81-\ntasks.md-82-<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n--\nplan.md:76:| `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\nplan.md-77-| `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\nplan.md-78-| `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\nplan.md-79-| `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\nplan.md-80-| `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\nplan.md-81-| Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\nplan.md-82-| `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n--\nspec.md:91:$ rg -n \"Command in the brief|COMMAND:\" AGENTS.md\nspec.md-92-(no output, exit 1)\nspec.md-93-\nspec.md-94-$ node P6/scratch/measure-policies.mjs\nspec.md-95-commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}\nspec.md-96-run records 20 non-read-only run: [\"/doctor:deep-loop deep-loop add-only\",\"/doctor:speckit speckit-retrieval add-only\"]\nspec.md-97-{\"command\":\"/doctor:git\",\"route\":\"hooks\",\"mutating\":\"mutates\",\"askFirst\":[],\"policy\":\"ask\"}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers && rg -n -A6 \\\"Command in the brief\\\" spec.md plan.md tasks.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524015774,"end":1794524016265}}}}
