{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524176283,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1f9aefc0013pZH4Y1792ZfnP","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1f9a6960011ojCYhxSwfn6Jc","type":"tool","id":"call_8b4481675dd145d7b76b937e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Research Strategy - performance lineage\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nPerformance and cost of command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008: where Claude hook wall time goes, what the brief and a started command cost in tokens, which cold-start path can exceed a runtime hook budget, and which caching or precompute change pays for itself across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Where does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\n- [ ] What does command surfacing cost in tokens per prompt, per session and per started command, and where is the largest avoidable cost?\n- [ ] Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\n- [ ] Which caching or precompute change pays for itself across the six CLIs, and which does not?\n- [ ] Which per-runtime architecture spends the least per prompt, and what should the other runtimes copy?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Changing skill scoring, thresholds or the meaning bar. Those are frozen by phase 004 and the parent decision record.\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan: recommendation fields and brief head, Gate 2 binding and pointers, per-runtime behaviour proof, embedder visibility, the 750 ms prompt deadline, the doctor routes and the install guide text.\n- Running any runtime CLI, pi, ollama lifecycle control, process kills, the full vitest suite, or a git write.\n- Reading holdout rows of command-prompts.jsonl or any corpus file with a holdout split.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Five iterations, or legal convergence after the three-iteration floor.\n- Every recommendation names the exact file it changes, a measured baseline and a verification command.\n- A measurement that the hard rules forbid is recorded as a gap, never guessed.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nIteration 1: decompose the measured Claude hook wall time into process starts, CLI call and hook work, and read the cold-start caps on the daemon path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nEvidence already read before iteration 1:\n- Hook latency, 44 tune prompts, pre and post the phase 004 meaning lane: before median 199.16/199.26/199.01 ms, p95 231.35/234.76/224.33; after median 206.23/194.83/205.09, p95 269.27/259.04/261.92 (`004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json`).\n- Warm query embedding 6.57 ms median, 10.99 ms p95 over 30 calls; advisor CLI call 62.7 to 71.3 ms over 5 calls; operator cold reading 271 to 277 ms per cold embed and 413 ms for one advisor CLI call with the model cold (`008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt`).\n- Claude per-prompt chain: `bash -c` -> spec-kit shim `node` (2500 ms child timeout) -> advisor hook `node` -> `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` -> daemon.\n- Hook budgets: Claude shim 2500 ms and CLI fallback default 250 ms; Pi 2500 ms in-process; DSH in-process; OpenCode plugin in-process with its own 5-minute exact-prompt cache.\n- Phase 008 plans a 750 ms prompt-embedding deadline and does not preload the model or keep it loaded.\n- Phase 005 adds `use <owner> -> <command> (<policy>)` to the brief head; phase 006 adds one Gate 2 bullet and may grow the delivery prefix by at most 463 bytes.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl` (not used in this lineage)\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-12T23:50:00.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Research Strategy - performance lineage\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nPerformance and cost of command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008: where Claude hook wall time goes, what the brief and a started command cost in tokens, which cold-start path can exceed a runtime hook budget, and which caching or precompute change pays for itself across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] Where does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\\n- [ ] What does command surfacing cost in tokens per prompt, per session and per started command, and where is the largest avoidable cost?\\n- [ ] Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\\n- [ ] Which caching or precompute change pays for itself across the six CLIs, and which does not?\\n- [ ] Which per-runtime architecture spends the least per prompt, and what should the other runtimes copy?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n- Changing skill scoring, thresholds or the meaning bar. Those are frozen by phase 004 and the parent decision record.\\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan: recommendation fields and brief head, Gate 2 binding and pointers, per-runtime behaviour proof, embedder visibility, the 750 ms prompt deadline, the doctor routes and the install guide text.\\n- Running any runtime CLI, pi, ollama lifecycle control, process kills, the full vitest suite, or a git write.\\n- Reading holdout rows of command-prompts.jsonl or any corpus file with a holdout split.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n- Five iterations, or legal convergence after the three-iteration floor.\\n- Every recommendation names the exact file it changes, a measured baseline and a verification command.\\n- A measurement that the hard rules forbid is recorded as a gap, never guessed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nIteration 1: decompose the measured Claude hook wall time into process starts, CLI call and hook work, and read the cold-start caps on the daemon path.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nEvidence already read before iteration 1:\\n- Hook latency, 44 tune prompts, pre and post the phase 004 meaning lane: before median 199.16/199.26/199.01 ms, p95 231.35/234.76/224.33; after median 206.23/194.83/205.09, p95 269.27/259.04/261.92 (`004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-*.json`).\\n- Warm query embedding 6.57 ms median, 10.99 ms p95 over 30 calls; advisor CLI call 62.7 to 71.3 ms over 5 calls; operator cold reading 271 to 277 ms per cold embed and 413 ms for one advisor CLI call with the model cold (`008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt`).\\n- Claude per-prompt chain: `bash -c` -> spec-kit shim `node` (2500 ms child timeout) -> advisor hook `node` -> `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` -> daemon.\\n- Hook budgets: Claude shim 2500 ms and CLI fallback default 250 ms; Pi 2500 ms in-process; DSH in-process; OpenCode plugin in-process with its own 5-minute exact-prompt cache.\\n- Phase 008 plans a 750 ms prompt-embedding deadline and does not preload the model or keep it loaded.\\n- Phase 005 adds `use <owner> -> <command> (<policy>)` to the brief head; phase 006 adds one Gate 2 bullet and may grow the delivery prefix by at most 463 bytes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl` (not used in this lineage)\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-12T23:50:00.000Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524163836,"end":1794524176283}}}}
