{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524290202,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fb986e001IN2Bpn6BjHY2Xh","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1fb902b0010upQ3ZL39QqJA0","type":"tool","id":"call_ed7da4ebcdf54f77a76a2ad2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/ANCHOR:answered-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -30; echo \"--- next focus:\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Where does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\n- [ ] What does command surfacing cost in tokens per prompt, per session and per started command, and where is the largest avoidable cost?\n- [ ] Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\n- [ ] Which caching or precompute change pays for itself across the six CLIs, and which does not?\n- [ ] Which per-runtime architecture spends the least per prompt, and what should the other runtimes copy?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Changing skill scoring, thresholds or the meaning bar. Those are frozen by phase 004 and the parent decision record.\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan: recommendation fields and brief head, Gate 2 binding and pointers, per-runtime behaviour proof, embedder visibility, the 750 ms prompt deadline, the doctor routes and the install guide text.\n- Running any runtime CLI, pi, ollama lifecycle control, process kills, the full vitest suite, or a git write.\n- Reading holdout rows of command-prompts.jsonl or any corpus file with a holdout split.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Five iterations, or legal convergence after the three-iteration floor.\n- Every recommendation names the exact file it changes, a measured baseline and a verification command.\n- A measurement that the hard rules forbid is recorded as a gap, never guessed.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n--- next focus:\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The phase 004 meaning lane moved the hook median by 5.9 ms but its p95 by 30.6 ms (middle run 199.16 to 205.09 ms median, 231.35 to 261.92 ms p95), and the warm query embedding it adds is only 6.57 ms median and 10.99...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Where does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\n- [ ] What does command surfacing cost in tokens per prompt, per session and per started command, and where is the largest avoidable cost?\n- [ ] Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\n- [ ] Which caching or precompute change pays for itself across the six CLIs, and which does not?\n- [ ] Which per-runtime architecture spends the least per prompt, and what should the other runtimes copy?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Changing skill scoring, thresholds or the meaning bar. Those are frozen by phase 004 and the parent decision record.\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005 to 008 already plan: recommendation fields and brief head, Gate 2 binding and pointers, per-runtime behaviour proof, embedder visibility, the 750 ms prompt deadline, the doctor routes and the install guide text.\n- Running any runtime CLI, pi, ollama lifecycle control, process kills, the full vitest suite, or a git write.\n- Reading holdout rows of command-prompts.jsonl or any corpus file with a holdout split.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Five iterations, or legal convergence after the three-iteration floor.\n- Every recommendation names the exact file it changes, a measured baseline and a verification command.\n- A measurement that the hard rules forbid is recorded as a gap, never guessed.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n--- next focus:\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The phase 004 meaning lane moved the hook median by 5.9 ms but its p95 by 30.6 ms (middle run 199.16 to 205.09 ms median, 231.35 to 261.92 ms p95), and the warm query embedding it adds is only 6.57 ms median and 10.99...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/ANCHOR:answered-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -30; echo \\\"--- next focus:\\\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524289134,"end":1794524290202}}}}
