ile specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/steer.md, lines 1-10\n1: # Lineage focus: performance\n2: \n3: Angle: performance and cost. Hook wall time (cold and warm), daemon vs no-daemon paths, embedder cost and cold start (use measure-embedder-cost.mjs and the measured-2026-11-12.txt file), token cost of the brief per prompt and per session, caching and precompute opportunities. Measure with commands that are read-only and do not start/stop ollama; report baseline and expected delta.\n4: \n5: Rulings from the lead (bind inside this lineage):\n6: - Phases 005-008 of the parent packet are PLANNED, not built. Read their plan.md and tasks.md first and do not re-recommend what they already plan.\n7: - Every recommendation names the exact file it changes, the measurable gain (with the number you measured or the baseline it moves) and the verification command or check.\n8: - Never read or print rows of command-prompts.jsonl or any corpus file whose split is holdout.\n9: - Do not run pi, do not touch ollama, do not kill processes, do not run the full vitest suite, read-only git only. A measurement you cannot take under these rules is recorded as a gap, not guessed.\n10: - Other lineages cover the other two angles; stay on yours and note cross-angle findings only briefly."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/steer.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524428303,"end":1794524428741}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524428757,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1fdb435001g44800HUGlGaVj","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d1fdaa34001bS3q3Bx1dT9UoQ","type":"tool","id":"call_3a70b23fa887426994f21cde","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance && sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \"--- answered:\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:answered-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:answered-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \"--- worked:\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:what-worked/,/\\/ANCHOR:what-worked/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -12"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The 30.6 ms p95 tail is not the cold model. A cold call costs 271 to 277 ms, so even three cold calls inside a 44-prompt set would push p95 to roughly 470 ms, not the observed 262 ms. The tail is steady-state variance...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n--- answered:\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n--- worked:\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- measuring a bare Node start on the same machine turned a plausible \"startup is slow\" story into a quantified share of the measured median. Reading both sides of the shim boundary found a concrete cap mismatch that no phase plan mentions. (iteration 1)\n- pricing the cold call against the deadline, rather than against zero, separated a latency tax from a failure. Reading the adapter's abort path turned 008's deadline from a policy into a mechanism with a concrete injection point. (iteration 2)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The 30.6 ms p95 tail is not the cold model. A cold call costs 271 to 277 ms, so even three cold calls inside a 44-prompt set would push p95 to roughly 470 ms, not the observed 262 ms. The tail is steady-state variance...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n--- answered:\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n--- worked:\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- measuring a bare Node start on the same machine turned a plausible \"startup is slow\" story into a quantified share of the measured median. Reading both sides of the shim boundary found a concrete cap mismatch that no phase plan mentions. (iteration 1)\n- pricing the cold call against the deadline, rather than against zero, separated a latency tax from a failure. Reading the adapter's abort path turned 008's deadline from a policy into a mechanism with a concrete injection point. (iteration 2)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance && sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \\\"--- answered:\\\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:answered-questions/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:answered-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \\\"--- worked:\\\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:what-worked/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:what-worked/p' deep-research-strategy.md | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524427317,"end":1794524428757}}}}
