{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794524654577,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"id":"prt_1d2012bf1001PRPuloAHtCAbta","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d20122c4001aDTYFRvXNdGH9p","type":"step-start","snapshot":"c5fecca5968560f196e69cf3ea058c07757badd8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524682385,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2015ebd00162l8V7yS3Q5ElP","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d20122c4001aDTYFRvXNdGH9p","type":"tool","id":"call_a3ea9525c7ee4f9db6c5e6f5","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Performance and cost of command surfacing — progressive synthesis\n\nLineage: `performance`. Scope: hook wall time, cold start, embedder cost, brief and command-read tokens, caching, and per-runtime cost across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh. Phases 005 to 008 of the parent packet are planned, not built; nothing below repeats what they already plan.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where the Claude hook time goes\n\nThe Claude prompt path starts three Node processes before any scoring: the `bash -c` wrapper starts the spec-kit shim, the shim `spawnSync`s the advisor hook, and the advisor hook spawns `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. A bare `node -e 0` start measured 36.85 ms median (min 22.90, max 47.31, n=15) on the same machine whose hook median is 205.09 ms. Three starts are roughly 100 to 110 ms of that median, before hook or scorer work.\n\nThe 205.09 ms median sits beside a 62.7 to 71.3 ms measured CLI call, which already includes one Node start. Removing the CLI process (speaking the existing JSON-RPC to the daemon in-process through the launcher bridge) should land the median near 165 to 170 ms.\n\nSources: `.claude/settings.json:149`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js:17-167`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:253`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:34`, `004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json`.\n\n## 2. Cold start: the caps disagree\n\nThe shim gives the advisor child a 2200 ms budget (2500 ms `CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS` minus a 300 ms margin) and kills it at 2500 ms, while the CLI may wait 5000 ms for a cold daemon. A daemon cold start between 2.2 s and 5 s fails open even though the CLI is still working. A recorded sandbox run hit exactly that shape at 2508 ms.\n\nThe cheap fix is not a bigger timeout. A Claude `SessionStart` group already exists with eight adapters and none warms the advisor; one detached `advisor_status --warm-only` call there moves the cold daemon start off the prompt path.\n\nThe embedder has a separate cold story: the adapter sends no `keep_alive`, so the measured model unloaded after four minutes forty-nine seconds. The next prompt then pays 271 to 277 ms against a 6.57 ms warm median. That fits phase 008's planned 750 ms deadline, so it is a latency tax, not a fail-open. Holding the model costs 335,733,063 bytes loaded plus a 46,256 KB server and a 352,144 KB runner, so a keep-alive must be priced against about 335 MB.\n\nPhase 008's deadline should be passed into the adapter, not raced around it: the adapter already has an `AbortController` and an instance `timeoutMs`, but `getAdapter(name)` takes no options, so a wrapper race would abandon a live 5000 ms request instead of aborting it.\n\nThe 30.6 ms p95 move from phase 004 is not a cold model: a cold call would push p95 to roughly 470 ms. It is bounded steady-state variance and is not worth chasing.\n\n## 3. Tokens: the brief is not the cost\n\nThe shipped renderer produces a 257-character brief: a 41-character head plus a 216-character directive block, 64 tokens at the repository's 4-chars-per-token estimate, 84% of it constant. Phase 005's command head takes that to 71 tokens. A 40-prompt session with one full brief and 39 reduced heads costs about 466 tokens today and about 734 with the command: a 268-token delta, 0.37% of a 200k context.\n\nA started command costs far more: the 44 tracked command documents have a median of 4,524 bytes (about 1,131 tokens), a p95 of 12,573 bytes (about 3,143 tokens) and a maximum of 13,682 bytes. Three starts cost 4.6 times a whole session's brief. The policy mix is 20 `start`, 17 `ask`, 7 `run`; an `ask` adds one model turn, the only material per-start cost, and phase 007 does not count turns.\n\nThe 84% directive-block saving is already built by the lifecycle dedup. Trimming the brief, a per-prompt token budget, or caching rendered briefs buys at most 54 tokens per session. Token cost is a negative result; the only guard worth building is visibility of a command document's read cost.\n\n## 4. Working recommendations so far\n\n| # | Recommendation | Files | Gain | Verify |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | Speak JSON-RPC to the daemon in-process instead of spawning the CLI from the hook | `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, keep `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` for cold start and fallback | one measured Node start, 36.85 ms median; hook median 205 → ~168 ms | `node 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` |\n| P2 | Warm the daemon at session start with one detached `advisor_status --warm-only` call | `.claude/settings.json` SessionStart group; per-runtime equivalents in `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` | first-prompt p95 from the 2500 ms ceiling to ~205 ms; zero first-prompt fail_open | hook-latency probe on a fresh session; diagnostic count of `fail_open` |\n| P3 | Add `keep_alive` to the query embed and warm the model once per session | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:343` plus an option on the adapter factory | cold first call 271–277 ms → ~7 ms; about 335 MB held while warm | `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` after a 10-minute idle: `cold.firstCallMs` null and `/api/ps` lists the model |\n| P4 | Thread the 750 ms prompt deadline into the adapter as a real timeout | `shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83`, `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts`, `lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:128` | the request aborts at 750 ms instead of 5 s, freeing the socket for the next prompt | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` plus a socket-close assertion |\n| P5 | Report the command-document read cost and flag a `start` row above 8 KB | new `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/measure-command-read-cost.mjs`, wired into the existing capture run | makes a future 3x document visible before it ships; today 5 docs exceed 8 KB and each needs a reason | run the script: it prints per-command bytes and lists the 5 over the cap |\n\nP1 to P4 are post-008 changes; P5 is reporting, not a runtime change.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/research.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/research.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/research.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Performance and cost of command surfacing — progressive synthesis\\n\\nLineage: `performance`. Scope: hook wall time, cold start, embedder cost, brief and command-read tokens, caching, and per-runtime cost across claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh. Phases 005 to 008 of the parent packet are planned, not built; nothing below repeats what they already plan.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Where the Claude hook time goes\\n\\nThe Claude prompt path starts three Node processes before any scoring: the `bash -c` wrapper starts the spec-kit shim, the shim `spawnSync`s the advisor hook, and the advisor hook spawns `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. A bare `node -e 0` start measured 36.85 ms median (min 22.90, max 47.31, n=15) on the same machine whose hook median is 205.09 ms. Three starts are roughly 100 to 110 ms of that median, before hook or scorer work.\\n\\nThe 205.09 ms median sits beside a 62.7 to 71.3 ms measured CLI call, which already includes one Node start. Removing the CLI process (speaking the existing JSON-RPC to the daemon in-process through the launcher bridge) should land the median near 165 to 170 ms.\\n\\nSources: `.claude/settings.json:149`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js:17-167`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:253`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:34`, `004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json`.\\n\\n## 2. Cold start: the caps disagree\\n\\nThe shim gives the advisor child a 2200 ms budget (2500 ms `CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS` minus a 300 ms margin) and kills it at 2500 ms, while the CLI may wait 5000 ms for a cold daemon. A daemon cold start between 2.2 s and 5 s fails open even though the CLI is still working. A recorded sandbox run hit exactly that shape at 2508 ms.\\n\\nThe cheap fix is not a bigger timeout. A Claude `SessionStart` group already exists with eight adapters and none warms the advisor; one detached `advisor_status --warm-only` call there moves the cold daemon start off the prompt path.\\n\\nThe embedder has a separate cold story: the adapter sends no `keep_alive`, so the measured model unloaded after four minutes forty-nine seconds. The next prompt then pays 271 to 277 ms against a 6.57 ms warm median. That fits phase 008's planned 750 ms deadline, so it is a latency tax, not a fail-open. Holding the model costs 335,733,063 bytes loaded plus a 46,256 KB server and a 352,144 KB runner, so a keep-alive must be priced against about 335 MB.\\n\\nPhase 008's deadline should be passed into the adapter, not raced around it: the adapter already has an `AbortController` and an instance `timeoutMs`, but `getAdapter(name)` takes no options, so a wrapper race would abandon a live 5000 ms request instead of aborting it.\\n\\nThe 30.6 ms p95 move from phase 004 is not a cold model: a cold call would push p95 to roughly 470 ms. It is bounded steady-state variance and is not worth chasing.\\n\\n## 3. Tokens: the brief is not the cost\\n\\nThe shipped renderer produces a 257-character brief: a 41-character head plus a 216-character directive block, 64 tokens at the repository's 4-chars-per-token estimate, 84% of it constant. Phase 005's command head takes that to 71 tokens. A 40-prompt session with one full brief and 39 reduced heads costs about 466 tokens today and about 734 with the command: a 268-token delta, 0.37% of a 200k context.\\n\\nA started command costs far more: the 44 tracked command documents have a median of 4,524 bytes (about 1,131 tokens), a p95 of 12,573 bytes (about 3,143 tokens) and a maximum of 13,682 bytes. Three starts cost 4.6 times a whole session's brief. The policy mix is 20 `start`, 17 `ask`, 7 `run`; an `ask` adds one model turn, the only material per-start cost, and phase 007 does not count turns.\\n\\nThe 84% directive-block saving is already built by the lifecycle dedup. Trimming the brief, a per-prompt token budget, or caching rendered briefs buys at most 54 tokens per session. Token cost is a negative result; the only guard worth building is visibility of a command document's read cost.\\n\\n## 4. Working recommendations so far\\n\\n| # | Recommendation | Files | Gain | Verify |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| P1 | Speak JSON-RPC to the daemon in-process instead of spawning the CLI from the hook | `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, keep `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` for cold start and fallback | one measured Node start, 36.85 ms median; hook median 205 → ~168 ms | `node 004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` |\\n| P2 | Warm the daemon at session start with one detached `advisor_status --warm-only` call | `.claude/settings.json` SessionStart group; per-runtime equivalents in `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md` | first-prompt p95 from the 2500 ms ceiling to ~205 ms; zero first-prompt fail_open | hook-latency probe on a fresh session; diagnostic count of `fail_open` |\\n| P3 | Add `keep_alive` to the query embed and warm the model once per session | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapters/ollama.ts:343` plus an option on the adapter factory | cold first call 271–277 ms → ~7 ms; about 335 MB held while warm | `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` after a 10-minute idle: `cold.firstCallMs` null and `/api/ps` lists the model |\\n| P4 | Thread the 750 ms prompt deadline into the adapter as a real timeout | `shared/embeddings/registry.ts:83`, `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts`, `lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts:128` | the request aborts at 750 ms instead of 5 s, freeing the socket for the next prompt | `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` plus a socket-close assertion |\\n| P5 | Report the command-document read cost and flag a `start` row above 8 KB | new `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/measure-command-read-cost.mjs`, wired into the existing capture run | makes a future 3x document visible before it ships; today 5 docs exceed 8 KB and each needs a reason | run the script: it prints per-command bytes and lists the 5 over the cap |\\n\\nP1 to P4 are post-008 changes; P5 is reporting, not a runtime change.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524667581,"end":1794524682385}}}}
