does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\",\n    \"Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\",\n  ],\n  answeredQuestions: [\n    \"Where does the ~205 ms Claude hook wall time go, and which part can be removed without changing the recommendation?\",\n    \"Which cold-start paths (daemon, embedder, first prompt of a session) can exceed the runtime's hook budget, and what removes the stall?\",\n  ],\n  ruledOut: [\"Any further cache or precompute project\", \"A performance explanation for the uneven start rates\", \"Re-opening the brief token budget\"],\n  focusTrack: \"performance\",\n  edgeCase: \"missing-dependency\",\n  toolsUsed: [\"Read\", \"Grep\"],\n  sourcesQueried: [\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md\",\n    \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json\",\n  ],\n  timestamp: ts,\n  durationMs: 300000,\n  graphEvents,\n};\nconst rows = [\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-001\", label: \"No performance recommendation repeats a planned phase: 005 changes fields and brief, 006 the Gate 2 text and pointers, 007 behaviour proof, 008 embedder visibility and a wrapper deadline; none changes hook transport, warms the daemon, adds keep_alive or reports read cost.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md:58\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/spec.md:157\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md:76\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-002\", label: \"Two removed process starts take the Claude median from 205.09 ms to about 131 ms, a 36 percent cut; every runtime gains at least one 36.85 ms start per prompt.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency-after-3.json:1\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-003\", label: \"The only fail-open path found is a cold daemon start between 2.2 s and 5 s on Claude and between 2.8 s and 5 s on Codex, which a session-start warm call removes.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js:137\", \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js:12\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:34\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-004\", label: \"Cold daemon start is the one unmeasured number; its procedure is a sandbox socket and database, five timed starts and a cold hook-latency run, never the live daemon.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/host-integrations/003-pi-skill-orchestrator-based-research-refinement/011-observation-fixes/evidence/goal-reverify/reports/pi-433.md:1\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-005\", label: \"Command surfacing adds about 7 tokens per brief and about 1,131 tokens per start, so no phase-005-to-008 code change is needed for cost; the ask turn is a UX decision already made.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:557\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/spec.md:94\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-006\", label: \"Performance does not explain the uneven start rates: claude 3 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 0 of 12, devin 2 of 12, opencode 4 of 9 and dsh 3 of 8 with one COMMAND line, on a hook path of the same order on every runtime.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl:1\"] },\n  { type: \"finding\", id: \"f-iter005-007\", label: \"Declined with reasons: semantic cache, cache persistence, new precompute, brief trimming, a per-prompt token budget and a longer cold timeout.\", iteration: 5, sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/prompt-cache.ts:16\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:23\"] },\n  { type: \"ruled_out\", id: \"ro-iter005-001\", direction: \"Any further cache or precompute project\", reason: \"The evidence does not support a payoff and the telemetry that would justify one is off by default.\", iteration: 5 },\n  { type: \"ruled_out\", id: \"ro-iter005-002\", direction: \"A performance explanation for the uneven start rates\", reason: \"The same hook cost applies to every runtime and the spread is behavioural.\", iteration: 5 },\n  { type: \"ruled_out\", id: \"ro-iter005-003\", direction: \"Re-open the brief token budget\", reason: \"The brief is below the cap and the constant block is already suppressed.\", iteration: 5 },\n];\nfs.writeFileSync(`${dir}/.gateway-events/iteration-005.json`, JSON.stringify(rec));\nfs.writeFileSync(`${dir}/deltas/iter-005.jsonl`, `${[rec, ...rows].map((r) => JSON.stringify(r)).join(\"\\n\")}\\n`);\nconsole.log(\"wrote\", ts);\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/