{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794524859435,"sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d20448cc0018vAYFva6eKsCcx","sessionID":"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O","messageID":"msg_1d2043c290017FxbNgbHeB0RHB","type":"tool","id":"call_f3acc8d57e984ee2a9eaddad","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages && ls -la ux cross-cli 2>/dev/null | head -30; echo \"--- ux research.md:\"; head -50 ux/research.md 2>/dev/null"},"output":"cross-cli:\ntotal 248\ndrwx------@ 22 michelkerkmeester  staff    704 Nov 13 00:07 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 23:47 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    512 Nov 12 23:52 .deep-research.lock\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 12 23:47 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 13 00:07 .legacy-projection-watermarks\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 12 23:47 containment\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-audit-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   2819 Nov 12 23:51 deep-research-config.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   6871 Nov 13 00:06 deep-research-dashboard.md\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 12 23:47 deep-research-effect-ledger\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   2749 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-state.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  20410 Nov 13 00:06 deep-research-strategy.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 13 00:04 deltas\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  41896 Nov 13 00:06 findings-registry.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    430 Nov 12 23:47 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 13 00:04 iterations\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 23:51 locks-and-fencing-v1\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 12 23:50 prompts\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  20982 Nov 13 00:07 research.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   5286 Nov 13 00:06 resource-map.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   1242 Nov 12 23:47 steer.md\n\nux:\ntotal 200\ndrwx------@ 21 michelkerkmeester  staff    672 Nov 12 23:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 23:47 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    503 Nov 12 23:54 .deep-research.lock\n--- ux research.md:\n# UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness after phases 005 to 008 — ux lineage\n\nDetached research lineage `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`. Topic: what to improve in command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle, with the cross-CLI start question as the spine. Every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain and the check that proves it. Phases 005 to 008 are planned, not built; nothing here repeats them.\n\n## 1. Executive verdict\n\n[Progressive — populated as iterations complete.]\n\n## 2. Answers to key questions\n\n- KQ1 What the brief emits and whether a model can act on it: **partly answered**. The brief is a 3-line, 240-296 character payload with a 320-character head budget, no document path and no offer state; the harness cannot distinguish an offer from a decline. See §3, findings 1-5.\n- KQ2 Which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates: open.\n- KQ3 Which discovery defects exist and what detects them: open.\n- KQ4 What an external repository sees on first run: open.\n- KQ5 What the brief and the hook cost: open.\n\n## 3. Findings by iteration\n\n### Iteration 1 — the model-visible brief\n\n1. The brief is 240-296 characters (about 60-74 tokens); 79 to 90 percent of a short brief is the same static directive block. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:162]\n2. The head uses 72 to 96 of its 320 available characters, leaving about 225 unused on every prompt. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:97]\n3. The brief names a command but never its document path; the 13 `create:*` commands have no Skill-tool route while `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n4. The closed diagnostic schema records `skillLabel` and `emittedBytes` but no offered command or policy, so an offer cannot be distinguished from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n\n### Iteration 2 — before-arm behaviour and the policy gap\n\n6. The aggregate start rate inverts by policy class: claude is 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; opencode and dsh are 3 of 8 `start` and 2 or 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n7. The start rate measures the path, not the outcome: devin produced `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` from `/create:agent` rows while scoring `started: false`; 5 of 8 mutating devin rows wrote. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n8. The run-or-ask policy stops at the command: devin created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi wrote a retrieval fixture on `ask` rows without asking, because the skill path that runs the same workflow carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n9. No before-arm start is attributable to the advisor; the brief names no command and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on four runtimes and 1 of 12 on dsh.\n\n### Iteration 3 — discovery surface\n\n10. Claude exposes 32 of 44 tracked commands: `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` collapses 13 files into one Skill entry, and the same file is mirrored into OpenCode's folder surface untested. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n11. The same command has three native spellings: `/create:readme` on Claude and OpenCode, `create-readme` on Cursor, Codex and Pi, and no command surface at all on Devin. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:202]\n12. No committed check measures per-runtime command visibility; the mirror check validates link shape only and covers two of six roots. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:53]\n\n## 4. Recommendations\n\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis. Iteration 1 candidates are in `iterations/iteration-001.md` under Recommendations.]\n\n## 5. Per-runtime notes\n\n| Runtime | Before-arm start | Split | Unsafe | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| claude | 3 of 12 | 3 of 4 `run`, 0 of 8 `start`, 0 of 4 `ask` | 0 | Adopts only checks it cannot improvise; Skill tool exposes 32 of 44 commands |\n| codex | 0 of 12 | 0 of 8, 0 of 4, 0 of 4 | 0 | No adoption; flat `create-readme` prompt surface |\n| opencode | 5 of 12 | 3 of 8 `start`, 2 of 4 `run` | 0 | Adopts mutating creation workflows; folder surface shares the `skill.md` risk |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"cross-cli:\ntotal 248\ndrwx------@ 22 michelkerkmeester  staff    704 Nov 13 00:07 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 23:47 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    512 Nov 12 23:52 .deep-research.lock\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 12 23:47 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 13 00:07 .legacy-projection-watermarks\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 12 23:47 containment\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-audit-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   2819 Nov 12 23:51 deep-research-config.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   6871 Nov 13 00:06 deep-research-dashboard.md\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 12 23:47 deep-research-effect-ledger\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   2749 Nov 13 00:07 deep-research-state.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  20410 Nov 13 00:06 deep-research-strategy.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 13 00:04 deltas\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  41896 Nov 13 00:06 findings-registry.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    430 Nov 12 23:47 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 13 00:04 iterations\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 12 23:51 locks-and-fencing-v1\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 12 23:50 prompts\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  20982 Nov 13 00:07 research.md\n-rw-------@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   5286 Nov 13 00:06 resource-map.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   1242 Nov 12 23:47 steer.md\n\nux:\ntotal 200\ndrwx------@ 21 michelkerkmeester  staff    672 Nov 12 23:58 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 michelkerkmeester  staff    160 Nov 12 23:47 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    503 Nov 12 23:54 .deep-research.lock\n--- ux research.md:\n# UX, performance and cross-CLI usefulness after phases 005 to 008 — ux lineage\n\nDetached research lineage `ux`, session `fanout-ux-1794523629654-v541y3`. Topic: what to improve in command surfacing after the planned phases 005 to 008, on the UX angle, with the cross-CLI start question as the spine. Every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain and the check that proves it. Phases 005 to 008 are planned, not built; nothing here repeats them.\n\n## 1. Executive verdict\n\n[Progressive — populated as iterations complete.]\n\n## 2. Answers to key questions\n\n- KQ1 What the brief emits and whether a model can act on it: **partly answered**. The brief is a 3-line, 240-296 character payload with a 320-character head budget, no document path and no offer state; the harness cannot distinguish an offer from a decline. See §3, findings 1-5.\n- KQ2 Which before-arm behaviour explains the start rates: open.\n- KQ3 Which discovery defects exist and what detects them: open.\n- KQ4 What an external repository sees on first run: open.\n- KQ5 What the brief and the hook cost: open.\n\n## 3. Findings by iteration\n\n### Iteration 1 — the model-visible brief\n\n1. The brief is 240-296 characters (about 60-74 tokens); 79 to 90 percent of a short brief is the same static directive block. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:162]\n2. The head uses 72 to 96 of its 320 available characters, leaving about 225 unused on every prompt. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:97]\n3. The brief names a command but never its document path; the 13 `create:*` commands have no Skill-tool route while `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n4. The closed diagnostic schema records `skillLabel` and `emittedBytes` but no offered command or policy, so an offer cannot be distinguished from a decline. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:50]\n5. An argued doctor route such as `/doctor:git hooks` can never be scored from its document read because `commandParts` keeps the argument in the name. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:449]\n\n### Iteration 2 — before-arm behaviour and the policy gap\n\n6. The aggregate start rate inverts by policy class: claude is 3 of 4 read-only `run` rows and 0 of 8 mutating `start` rows; opencode and dsh are 3 of 8 `start` and 2 or 1 of 4 `run`; codex is 0 of 8 and 0 of 4. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n7. The start rate measures the path, not the outcome: devin produced `.skilled/agents/dependency-audit.md`, `.claude/agents/dependency-audit.md` and `.devin/agents/dependency-audit/` from `/create:agent` rows while scoring `started: false`; 5 of 8 mutating devin rows wrote. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl]\n8. The run-or-ask policy stops at the command: devin created `specs/sk-prompt/010-sk-prompt-improvements/scratch/council/` and pi wrote a retrieval fixture on `ask` rows without asking, because the skill path that runs the same workflow carries no policy. [SOURCE: AGENTS.md:63]\n9. No before-arm start is attributable to the advisor; the brief names no command and `COMMAND:` narration is 0 of 24 on four runtimes and 1 of 12 on dsh.\n\n### Iteration 3 — discovery surface\n\n10. Claude exposes 32 of 44 tracked commands: `.claude/commands/create/skill.md` collapses 13 files into one Skill entry, and the same file is mirrored into OpenCode's folder surface untested. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt]\n11. The same command has three native spellings: `/create:readme` on Claude and OpenCode, `create-readme` on Cursor, Codex and Pi, and no command surface at all on Devin. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:202]\n12. No committed check measures per-runtime command visibility; the mirror check validates link shape only and covers two of six roots. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:53]\n\n## 4. Recommendations\n\n[Progressive — consolidated at synthesis. Iteration 1 candidates are in `iterations/iteration-001.md` under Recommendations.]\n\n## 5. Per-runtime notes\n\n| Runtime | Before-arm start | Split | Unsafe | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| claude | 3 of 12 | 3 of 4 `run`, 0 of 8 `start`, 0 of 4 `ask` | 0 | Adopts only checks it cannot improvise; Skill tool exposes 32 of 44 commands |\n| codex | 0 of 12 | 0 of 8, 0 of 4, 0 of 4 | 0 | No adoption; flat `create-readme` prompt surface |\n| opencode | 5 of 12 | 3 of 8 `start`, 2 of 4 `run` | 0 | Adopts mutating creation workflows; folder surface shares the `skill.md` risk |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages && ls -la ux cross-cli 2>/dev/null | head -30; echo \\\"--- ux research.md:\\\"; head -50 ux/research.md 2>/dev/null\"}"},"time":{"start":1794524858572,"end":1794524859435}}}}
